// Offline copy of the Google Sheet, used when the sheet is not connected or cannot be reached.
// Generated by tools/build-local-data.mjs from CSV files - edit the CSVs (or the sheet), not this file.
window.LOCAL_CSV = {
  "settings": "key,value,note\ncompany_name,KLAE Group,\"Shown in the header, footer and page titles.\"\nsite_title,Synology Package Guide,\nintro,\"What each package on our Synology NAS does, which department it is for, and how to start using it. Maintained by IT.\",Text under the main heading on the overview page.\nlogo_url,,\"Optional. Path or link to the company logo, e.g. assets/img/logo.png. Empty = text mark.\"\nnas_url,,\"DSM sign-in address, e.g. https://nas.company.local:5001. Never put passwords in this sheet.\"\ndrive_url,,\"Synology Drive web address, if different from the DSM address.\"\ngetting_started,\"Ask IT for a DSM account if you do not have one yet.\nSign in to the NAS in a web browser with the address IT gives you.\nTurn on 2-step sign-in when you are asked to (Secure SignIn).\nInstall Synology Drive Client on your PC, and the Synology Drive app on your phone if you need files on the move.\nSave work files in your team folder, not on your desktop, so they are backed up and colleagues can find them.\",One step per line (Alt+Enter in the cell).\npolicy,\"Only packages published by Synology Inc. are approved for general use at KLAE Group.\nPackages from other publishers (\"\"contributors\"\"), including community package sources added under Package Center > Settings > Package Sources, must not be installed. Their developers can stop updating them at any time, and Synology does not support them.\nPackages in the Open Source section (for example Apache, PHP, Node.js and WordPress) are developed by outside open-source projects but packaged and published by Synology Inc. They are for the IT and Software Engineering teams only, and need IT approval first.\nStaff do not install, update or remove packages. Send a request to IT. IT checks the business need, licence cost, security and storage impact before installing anything.\nIT keeps the Package Center trust level at \"\"Synology Inc.\"\" (Package Center > Settings > General > Trust Level) so that unsigned or third-party packages cannot be installed by mistake.\",One paragraph per line.\npolicy_short,\"Only packages published by Synology Inc. are approved. Third-party and community packages are not allowed, and open-source packages need IT approval.\",One line shown on the overview page.\nit_contact_name,IT Department,\nit_contact_email,,\nit_contact_phone,,Phone or extension.\nrequest_form_url,,Optional. Google Form link for access or package requests.\nlast_reviewed,2026-10-20,Update this when you review the guide.\nshow_nas_status,no,\"yes = show install status, installed versions and do-not-uninstall warnings. Keep no on the public site.\"\n",
  "apps": "id,name,icon,section,developer,publisher,category,on_our_nas,approval,approval_note,user_type,departments,summary,description,use_cases,how_to,tips,access,related,depends_on,keywords,installed_version,version,learn_more\nactive-backup-for-business,Active Backup for Business,icons/active-backup-for-business.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Backup, Business\",,Approved,Recommended for protecting staff laptops and servers; install version 3.2.1-25059 or later.,IT admin,it,\"Central, licence-free backup of company PCs, Macs, servers, virtual machines and file servers to the NAS.\",\"Active Backup for Business backs up Windows and Mac computers, physical servers, VMware and Hyper-V virtual machines, and file servers to the NAS from one console. It keeps deduplicated, versioned backups on a schedule and can restore anything from a single file to a whole machine. There are no per-device licence fees on supported Synology models.\",\"Engineering: back up the laptops field engineers take to commissioning sites, so a lost or damaged laptop does not lose project files and HMI programs.\nFinance: back up the PC that runs the accounting software every night, so it can be restored in full after a disk failure or ransomware.\nSWE: back up development servers and Hyper-V or VMware test VMs, and restore a whole VM after a failed update.\nIT: let staff restore their own deleted files through the Active Backup for Business Portal instead of raising a request.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Active Backup for Business and click Install; SMB Service, which it depends on, is set up with it.\nOpen Active Backup for Business from Main Menu and activate it with the company IT Synology Account when asked.\nMake sure backups go to a shared folder on a Btrfs volume, then set the default schedule and retention under Settings > Template.\nInstall the Active Backup for Business Agent from the Synology Download Center on each Windows PC or Mac, enter the NAS address and a DSM account, and check the device appears in the PC tab.\nFor virtual machines, open the Virtual Machine tab, add the VMware vSphere or Microsoft Hyper-V host, and create a backup task for the VMs you need.\nFor file servers, open the File Server tab, add the server's SMB or rsync details and create a task.\nAfter the first backup, test a restore through the Active Backup for Business Portal and create recovery media for full-machine restores.\",\"Install version 3.2.1-25059 or later: it fixes CVE-2026-15716 and Hyper-V backups and restores that fail after a Windows Defender update.\nBackups on the same NAS are not offsite. Copy them to another site or to Synology C2 with Hyper Backup.\nFull-machine backups use a lot of disk space and bandwidth; schedule them after office hours and watch volume usage in Storage Manager.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal, Desktop app, Background service\",\"active-backup-for-business-agent, hyper-backup, smb-service, snapshot-replication, storage-manager\",smb-service,\"backup pc, laptop backup, server backup, vm backup, restore files, ransomware recovery, hyper-v, vmware, abb\",,3.2.1-25059,\nactive-backup-for-business-agent,Active Backup for Business Agent (DSM),icons/active-backup-for-business-agent.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Backup,,IT approval needed,Needs a second Synology NAS running Active Backup for Business as the backup target.,IT admin,it,\"Backs up our whole NAS, including settings and packages, to a second NAS running Active Backup for Business.\",\"Active Backup for Business Agent (DSM) lets a Synology NAS back itself up in full, including system configuration, packages and user data. The backups go to a remote Synology NAS running Active Backup for Business, which stores and manages the versions. It is meant for rebuilding a whole NAS after a hardware failure or disaster.\",\"IT: keep a full image of the Puchong HQ NAS on a second Synology NAS at another office, so the whole system can be rebuilt after a fire, flood or hardware failure.\nManagement: shorten downtime after a major NAS failure, because settings and packages come back together with the data.\nFinance: get the accounting shared folders and their permissions back in one restore, without IT re-creating them by hand.\",\"Check on Synology's compatibility page that our NAS model supports Active Backup for Business Agent (DSM); it needs DSM 7.2 or later.\nOn the backup NAS, install Active Backup for Business and review the default settings for DSM backups under Settings > Template.\nOn the NAS you want to protect, go to Main Menu > Package Center, install Active Backup for Business Agent (DSM) and open it.\nClick Start, enter the backup NAS address (IP or domain name) and an account on it, then click Connect.\nRestart DSM when prompted to apply the settings, ideally after office hours.\nOn the backup NAS, confirm in Active Backup for Business that the first backup finished.\",\"A full-system backup can only be restored to the same NAS model or its successor, with at least as many drives in the same slots.\nPut the backup NAS in a different office or building, so one site problem cannot destroy both units.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"active-backup-for-business, hyper-backup, hyper-backup-vault, migration-assistant\",,\"nas backup, full system backup, disaster recovery, backup whole nas, nas image, abb agent, restore nas\",,2.5.2-12503,\nactive-backup-for-google-workspace,Active Backup for Google Workspace,icons/active-backup-for-google-workspace.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Backup,,Approved,Free on supported Synology NAS models; set it up only if KLAE's email and files run on Google Workspace.,IT admin,it,\"Backs up company Google Workspace mail, Drive, shared drives, calendars and contacts to the NAS.\",\"Active Backup for Google Workspace copies Gmail, Google Drive (My Drive and shared drives), Contacts and Calendar for company accounts onto the NAS. It can run in continuous backup mode or on a schedule, and keeps versions so deleted or overwritten items can be recovered. Staff can browse and restore their own items through a web portal.\",\"Sales: recover a customer email thread or a quotation in Google Drive that was deleted by mistake or lost when a salesperson left.\nHR: keep a copy of a departing employee's mailbox and Drive files after the Google account is removed.\nManagement: hold an independent copy of company email and documents outside Google, in case an account is compromised.\nIT: let staff restore their own files and emails through the portal instead of raising a request.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Active Backup for Google Workspace and click Install; Universal Search is installed with it.\nFollow the package's setup guide to create a Google service account with the required API access and domain-wide delegation in the Google Cloud and Google Admin consoles.\nOpen Active Backup for Google Workspace, create a task, and enter the Google Workspace admin email and the service account key file.\nSelect the services (Drive, shared drives, Gmail, Contacts, Calendar) and the accounts to protect, and turn on auto-discovery so new staff accounts are added.\nChoose continuous or scheduled backup and set a retention policy.\nTell staff they can open the Active Backup for Google Workspace Portal to browse and restore their own items.\",\"The service account can read every company mailbox and Drive, so only IT should hold its key file.\nThe first backup of large mailboxes and Drives takes a long time and needs plenty of NAS space.\nIf KLAE uses Microsoft 365 rather than Google Workspace, use Active Backup for Microsoft 365 instead.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal, Background service\",\"active-backup-for-microsoft-365, active-backup-for-business, universal-search, hyper-backup\",universal-search,\"gmail backup, google drive backup, google workspace, restore email, deleted email, shared drive, g suite\",,2.3.0-14256,\nactive-backup-for-microsoft-365,Active Backup for Microsoft 365,icons/active-backup-for-microsoft-365.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Backup,,Approved,\"Free on supported Synology NAS models; set it up only if KLAE uses Microsoft 365, and keep it on version 3.0.0 or later.\",IT admin,it,\"Backs up company Microsoft 365 email, OneDrive, SharePoint and Teams data to the NAS for easy recovery.\",\"Active Backup for Microsoft 365 copies Exchange Online mail, calendars and contacts, OneDrive for Business, SharePoint Online sites and Microsoft Teams data onto the NAS. It keeps versions so deleted or overwritten items can be restored, and staff can recover their own items through a web portal. Version 3.0.0 moves mail, calendar and contacts backup to Microsoft Graph ahead of Microsoft's October 2026 retirement of Exchange Web Services (EWS).\",\"Sales: recover a customer email or quotation attachment deleted from Outlook or OneDrive, even after the Microsoft recycle bin has been emptied.\nHR: keep a former employee's mailbox and OneDrive files after the Microsoft 365 licence is removed.\nEngineering: restore a SharePoint or Teams folder of commissioning reports after files are overwritten or deleted.\nManagement: hold a copy of company email and documents outside Microsoft, in case an account is compromised or ransomware syncs into OneDrive.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Active Backup for Microsoft 365 and click Install; Universal Search is installed with it.\nOpen Active Backup for Microsoft 365, create a task and sign in with a Microsoft 365 global administrator so the wizard can register the app in Microsoft Entra ID.\nSelect the services (mail, calendar, contacts, OneDrive, SharePoint, Teams) and the accounts to protect, and turn on auto-discovery for new staff.\nSet the backup schedule and retention policy.\nGive staff permission to use the Active Backup for Microsoft 365 Portal so they can browse and restore their own items.\nCheck the task status and logs after the first backup completes.\",\"Microsoft retires EWS in October 2026. Update to version 3.0.0 or later and update the Entra ID app credentials in each task, or mail backups and restores may fail.\nOnce EWS is disabled, restores to Exchange use Mailbox Import; some other services still use EWS during the transition.\nThe admin and app credentials give access to every mailbox, so only IT should hold them.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal, Background service\",\"active-backup-for-google-workspace, active-backup-for-business, universal-search, hyper-backup\",universal-search,\"outlook backup, email backup, onedrive backup, sharepoint backup, teams backup, office 365, restore email, exchange\",,3.0.0-14300,\nactive-insight,Active Insight,icons/active-insight.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Approved,It shares system health and performance data with Synology's cloud.,IT admin,it,Synology cloud service that watches NAS health and performance and warns IT before problems grow.,\"Active Insight sends health, performance and event data from the NAS to Synology's cloud, where IT can see dashboards and receive automated warnings. It can monitor several Synology systems in one place and helps Synology technical support diagnose problems faster.\",\"IT: get a warning when a drive shows errors, a volume is nearly full or performance drops, before staff notice.\nIT: watch the HQ NAS and any NAS at regional offices from one web dashboard, without logging in to each one.\nManagement: get faster answers from Synology support when there is a NAS problem.\nFinance: avoid surprise downtime of accounting folders at month-end, because IT is warned early about failing hardware.\",\"Open Main Menu > Active Insight on the NAS and sign in with the company IT Synology Account.\nGo to insight.synology.com and sign in with the same Synology Account to see the dashboard for our NAS.\nIn the notification settings, add the email addresses of everyone in the IT team so alerts do not depend on one person.\nReview the performance graphs and event history when staff report slowness or errors.\nMention Active Insight when opening a Synology support ticket, so support can use the collected data.\",\"Use a shared IT Synology Account rather than a personal one.\nIt sends system and performance data to Synology's cloud; confirm this fits KLAE's data policy.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal, Background service\",\"log-center, storage-manager, central-management-system, storage-analyzer\",,\"monitoring, nas health, alerts, performance, disk failure warning, support ticket, system status\",,3.0.6-24124,\nactiveprotect-vault,ActiveProtect Vault,icons/activeprotect-vault.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Backup,,Not recommended,No business need unless KLAE buys Synology ActiveProtect backup appliances.,IT admin,it,\"Remote, tamper-proof backup storage for Synology ActiveProtect appliances; not useful without them.\",\"ActiveProtect Vault turns a Synology NAS into remote storage for Synology ActiveProtect, a separate line of dedicated backup appliances. It keeps backup copies in WORM (write once, read many) vaults that cannot be changed before their retention ends, limits access to administrators, and lets IT choose the TLS encryption level. It runs on Container Manager.\",\"IT: only if KLAE later buys ActiveProtect appliances, keep a second, unchangeable copy of their backups on a NAS at another office.\nManagement: meet a customer or auditor requirement for backups that cannot be altered or deleted, if ActiveProtect is adopted.\nIT: for now, protect PCs, servers and shared folders with Active Backup for Business and Hyper Backup, which need no extra appliances.\",\"Confirm KLAE runs Synology ActiveProtect appliances; without them this package has no use.\nOn the NAS that will hold the copies, install Container Manager and then ActiveProtect Vault from Main Menu > Package Center.\nOpen ActiveProtect Vault, create a vault and choose its retention and TLS level.\nAdd the vault as a remote destination in the ActiveProtect appliance's management console.\nKeep the number of DSM administrator accounts small, since only administrators can access the vault.\",\"WORM data cannot be deleted before its retention ends, even by IT, so plan the space carefully.\nIt needs Container Manager, which uses extra RAM and CPU.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"container-manager, active-backup-for-business, hyper-backup, hyper-backup-vault\",container-manager,\"activeprotect, worm, immutable backup, backup vault, ransomware protection, tamper proof\",,2.0.0-2418,\nadvanced-media-extensions,Advanced Media Extensions,icons/advanced-media-extensions.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Multimedia, Productivity\",,Not recommended,\"Since version 4.0 the NAS no longer decodes these formats, so it adds little for KLAE.\",IT admin,it,\"Video codec add-on; since version 4.0, H.264/H.265 decoding happens on your own device instead.\",\"Advanced Media Extensions (AME) adds media codec support to DSM. From version 4.0.0-4025, processing of HEVC (H.265), AVC (H.264) and VC-1 media moved from the NAS to the viewing device, so files only play if that computer or phone supports the codec. AME 4.0 needs DSM 7.2.2 or later, and Surveillance Station uses Surveillance Video Extension for server-side H.264 instead.\",\"Marketing: product and exhibition videos in H.264 or H.265 play on staff PCs and phones that support those codecs, with or without AME.\nEngineering: save training-centre recordings as standard MP4 (H.264) so any device can play them.\nIT: install AME only if a Synology package lists it as required.\",\"Check whether any installed package actually requires it; normal file sharing does not need it.\nIf one does, install it from Package Center.\nFor iPhone HEIC photos or HEVC videos without previews in Synology Photos, install Synology Image Assistant on staff computers instead.\nFor camera recordings, use Surveillance Video Extension with Surveillance Station rather than AME.\",\"If the viewing device does not support the codec, playback of those files is limited.\nVideo Station was removed in DSM 7.2.2, so there is no video-library use for AME on DSM 7.2.2 or later.\",Background service,\"synology-photos, surveillance-video-extension, media-server, audio-station, universal-viewer\",,\"codec, hevc, h.265, h.264, heic, video playback, media codec, ame\",,4.0.0-4025,\nantivirus-by-mcafee,Antivirus by McAfee,icons/antivirus-by-mcafee.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Security,,IT approval needed,Paid licence after the trial; compare it with the free Antivirus Essential before buying.,IT admin,it,Paid antivirus that scans the NAS for viruses and malware using the McAfee engine.,\"Antivirus by McAfee scans the data and system partitions of the NAS for viruses and other malware, using McAfee's commercial scanning engine. IT can run manual scans or set scheduled scans, and virus definitions update automatically. It is a paid package with a free trial; version 1.6.1-4006 fixes false positives.\",\"Sales: scan the shared quotation and customer folders so a file infected on one laptop is not passed on to customers or principals.\nEngineering: check the folders where field engineers upload files copied from customer site PCs and USB drives after commissioning work.\nFinance: lower the risk that an infected invoice or bank statement attachment saved to the NAS spreads to other staff PCs.\nIT: run a scheduled full scan every weekend with a commercial engine, with virus definitions kept up to date automatically.\",\"If Antivirus Essential is installed, uninstall it first, because only one antivirus package should run at a time.\nGo to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Antivirus by McAfee and click Try to start the free trial.\nOpen Antivirus by McAfee from Main Menu and run a full scan to get a baseline.\nSet up a scheduled scan for nights or weekends, outside office hours.\nCheck that automatic virus-definition updates are turned on.\nReview any infected files the scans find, and buy a licence before the trial ends if KLAE decides to keep the package.\",\"Run only one antivirus package on the NAS at a time; do not install it alongside Antivirus Essential.\nFull scans use a lot of CPU and disk activity; schedule them outside office hours.\nAntivirus does not replace backups; recovery from ransomware still depends on snapshots and Hyper Backup.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"antivirus-essential, snapshot-replication, hyper-backup, log-center\",,\"antivirus, virus scan, malware, mcafee, virus, security scan, infected file, trojan\",,1.6.1-4006,\nantivirus-essential,Antivirus Essential,icons/antivirus-essential.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Security,,Approved,Free Synology package; it needs at least 1 GB of RAM to run scans.,IT admin,it,\"Free antivirus that scans NAS files for viruses and malware, on demand or on a schedule.\",\"Antivirus Essential is Synology's free antivirus package, based on the open-source ClamAV engine (upgraded to ClamAV 1.4.4 in version 1.6.1-4006). It runs full, custom or system scans, moves infected files to quarantine and updates virus definitions automatically. The latest version also fixes CVE-2026-20031 and some false positives.\",\"Sales: scan shared folders of quotations, tenders and customer drawings so infected files are not emailed to customers.\nEngineering: run a custom scan on the folder where engineers upload files from customer site PCs and USB drives.\nMarketing: check folders of exhibition material and brochure files received from printers and agencies.\nIT: run a weekly scheduled full scan and keep a record of anything found or quarantined.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Antivirus Essential and click Install.\nOpen Antivirus Essential and go to Update to download the latest virus definitions.\nOn Overview, choose Full scan for the whole NAS, Custom scan for chosen shared folders, or System scan for system areas.\nGo to Scheduled Scan and create a weekly full scan outside office hours.\nCheck Quarantine after each scan; delete infected files or restore any that are false positives.\nUse Logs to review past scans and Settings to adjust scan options.\",\"Scanning needs at least 1 GB of RAM and uses CPU; schedule full scans at night or on weekends.\nRun only one antivirus package at a time; do not install Antivirus by McAfee alongside it.\nKeep the package updated, as new versions fix security issues such as CVE-2026-20031.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"antivirus-by-mcafee, snapshot-replication, hyper-backup, log-center\",,\"antivirus, virus scan, free antivirus, malware, clamav, quarantine, virus, security scan\",,1.6.1-4006,\naudio-station,Audio Station,icons/audio-station.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Multimedia,,Not recommended,Entertainment app with no business need; store audio files in Synology Drive instead.,End user,marketing,Music library and streaming app; no business use at KLAE.,\"Audio Station organises music and audio files stored on the NAS for playback in the browser and on phones through the DS audio app. It supports playlists, internet radio and sharing. It is designed for home media use rather than office work.\",\"Marketing: voice-overs and audio for product videos can be stored and previewed in Synology Drive without this app.\nHR: background music for company events is easier to play from a laptop than to stream from the NAS.\nIT: not installing it keeps personal music off company storage and means one less package to patch.\",\"Check with IT first; it is not recommended at KLAE.\nIf IT installs it for a specific need, open Main Menu > Audio Station; it lists audio files from the music shared folder.\nBrowse by album, artist or folder, and double-click a track to play it in the browser.\nCreate playlists, or use the DS audio mobile app to play the library on a phone.\",Do not store personal music on company storage; it takes backup space and may raise copyright issues.,\"DSM web (Main Menu), Mobile app\",\"media-server, advanced-media-extensions, synology-drive-server\",,\"music, audio, mp3, songs, playlist, streaming, radio, ds audio\",,7.2.1-6006,\nbitdefender-for-mailplus,Bitdefender for MailPlus,icons/bitdefender-for-mailplus.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Security,,IT approval needed,Needs paid Bitdefender licences; weigh the cost against how much spam and malware we receive.,IT admin,it,Adds paid Bitdefender anti-spam and anti-virus engines to a Synology MailPlus company email server.,\"Bitdefender for MailPlus adds Bitdefender's commercial anti-spam and anti-virus engines to Synology MailPlus Server, so email is checked by Bitdefender for spam and viruses. It needs paid Bitdefender licences, which can be bought in advance with a chosen activation date. Version 1.1.0-20108 requires MailPlus Server 4.0.0 and DSM 7.2 or later.\",\"Finance: catch more phishing emails with fake payment requests or changed bank details before they reach accounts staff.\nSales: reduce spam in enquiry and quotation mailboxes, so real customer RFQs are not buried.\nHR: block malware hidden in attachments sent as job applications and CVs.\nIT: add a commercial filtering engine when company email runs on MailPlus Server.\",\"In Main Menu > Package Center, check that Synology MailPlus Server is version 4.0.0 or later; update it first if needed.\nSearch Package Center for Bitdefender for MailPlus and click Install.\nBuy Bitdefender licences for MailPlus; for a renewal, choose an activation date that starts when the current licence ends.\nActivate the licences on the NAS, then open Synology MailPlus Server and turn on the Bitdefender anti-spam and anti-virus engines in its security settings.\nSend a test email with the harmless EICAR antivirus test file and confirm it is blocked.\nAsk staff to report spam that still gets through, and adjust the filter settings.\",\"Licences can be bought ahead of time with a chosen activation date, so renewals do not leave a gap in protection.\nIt requires MailPlus Server 4.0.0 and DSM 7.2 or later; check versions before buying licences.\nNo filter catches everything; staff should still confirm by phone before paying a new invoice or changing a supplier's bank details.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"synology-mailplus-server, synology-mailplus, antivirus-essential, antivirus-by-mcafee\",synology-mailplus-server,\"spam, email virus, anti-spam, phishing, bitdefender, junk mail, email security, mailplus\",,1.1.0-20108,\nc2-identity-edge-server,C2 Identity Edge Server,icons/c2-identity-edge-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Management,,Not recommended,No use today; consider it only if KLAE subscribes to Synology C2 Identity.,IT admin,it,\"Local helper for Synology C2 Identity cloud accounts, so the NAS can check sign-ins quickly on site.\",\"Synology C2 Identity is a cloud directory service for managing staff accounts. C2 Identity Edge Server runs on the NAS and retrieves directory information from C2 Identity, so that when C2 Identity users access on-premises resources, the NAS can authenticate them quickly. It is only relevant if KLAE adopts C2 Identity.\",\"IT: if KLAE moves to C2 Identity, let staff at each regional office sign in to the local NAS with fast on-site authentication.\nHR: with C2 Identity, create or disable a staff account once in the cloud and have the change apply to the NAS at every office.\nSales: use the same company account to open shared folders on a regional office NAS as at Puchong HQ.\nManagement: compare C2 Identity with Synology Directory Server before choosing one company-wide account system.\",\"Decide first whether KLAE will use Synology C2 Identity; without it this package has no use.\nSet up the KLAE domain and staff accounts in the C2 Identity admin console.\nGo to Main Menu > Package Center, search for C2 Identity Edge Server and click Install.\nOpen C2 Identity Edge Server and follow its setup to link the NAS to the KLAE C2 Identity domain.\nTest that a C2 Identity user can sign in to the NAS and open the right shared folders.\",\"C2 Identity is a paid cloud service; get management approval before setting it up.\nChoose one directory system for the company: C2 Identity, Synology Directory Server or LDAP Server. Running several makes accounts harder to manage.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"synology-directory-server, ldap-server, sso-server, radius-server\",,\"c2 identity, user accounts, cloud directory, login, single account, domain, identity, edge server\",,1.78.0-0324,\ncentral-management-system,Central Management System,icons/central-management-system.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Utilities, Management\",,IT approval needed,\"Only useful if KLAE runs more than one Synology NAS, such as at regional offices.\",IT admin,it,\"Manages several Synology NAS from one console: monitoring, shared settings, updates and delegated admin.\",\"Central Management System (CMS) lets IT monitor and manage multiple Synology NAS from one host NAS. IT can group servers, create policies to change settings across a group at once, keep DSM and packages up to date, and delegate admin permissions per group or server. It is only useful when a company runs several Synology NAS, for example one per office.\",\"IT: apply the same security, password and notification settings to every office NAS from HQ.\nIT: roll out DSM and package updates to all office NAS units without logging in to each one.\nIT: let a local IT contact at a regional office manage only that office's NAS, through delegated permissions.\nManagement: be sure every office NAS follows the same security standard.\",\"Choose one NAS (normally at HQ) as the CMS host and install Central Management System from Main Menu > Package Center (it needs DSM 7.2-64570 or later).\nOpen Central Management System and add each managed NAS with its address and an administrator account.\nOrganise the servers into groups, for example by office.\nCreate policies to apply the same settings to each group.\nUse the update features to keep DSM and packages current across groups.\nDelegate admin permissions per group or server where a local contact needs them, and check the overview for offline or unhealthy servers.\",\"The CMS host has admin access to every NAS; protect its admin accounts with 2-factor authentication.\nConnect remote office NAS units over a VPN, not by opening admin ports to the internet.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"active-insight, log-center, vpn-server, synology-directory-server\",,\"manage multiple nas, central management, branch office, policy, mass update, cms, regional office nas\",,3.2.1-1259,\ncloud-sync,Cloud Sync,icons/cloud-sync.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Backup, Business, Productivity\",,IT approval needed,\"Each task sends company files to an outside cloud account, so IT reviews and sets up every link.\",IT admin,it,\"Keeps NAS folders in sync with cloud services such as OneDrive, SharePoint, Google Drive and Dropbox.\",\"Cloud Sync connects shared folders on the NAS with public cloud storage such as Microsoft OneDrive, Microsoft SharePoint, Google Drive, Google shared drives, Dropbox and Baidu Cloud. Each task can sync both ways, download only or upload only, with schedules, file filters and optional encryption. It keeps files the same in both places but is not a backup.\",\"Sales: download-only sync of a principal's shared OneDrive or SharePoint price list folder into the NAS, so every office sees the latest prices.\nMarketing: upload-only sync of final brochures and product photos to a Dropbox or Google Drive folder shared with the website agency.\nEngineering: pull principals' updated datasheets and manuals from their cloud folders into the engineering library on the NAS.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Cloud Sync and click Install, then open it.\nChoose the cloud provider and sign in with a company-owned cloud account, never a personal one.\nSelect the local shared folder and the remote folder to link.\nChoose the sync direction (both ways, download only or upload only) and turn on data encryption if needed.\nSet the schedule and file filters in the task settings.\nCheck the task status and history after the first sync.\",\"Cloud Sync is not a backup: deleted or ransomware-encrypted files can sync to the other side. Use Hyper Backup for backups.\nA Google shared drive holds at most 400,000 files and folders and up to 20 levels of subfolders; split large folders before syncing.\nA large first sync can use a lot of internet bandwidth; run it after office hours.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"hyper-backup, hybrid-share, synology-drive-server, active-backup-for-microsoft-365\",,\"onedrive, sharepoint, google drive, dropbox, cloud sync, sync to cloud, share with agency\",,2.7.3-2721,\ndhcp-server,DHCP Server,icons/dhcp-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,IT approval needed,Changes how a whole network gets IP addresses; a second DHCP server can cut staff off the network.,IT admin,it,\"Lets the NAS hand out IP addresses to devices on a network, a job the office router usually does.\",\"DHCP Server lets the NAS automatically assign IP addresses, gateway and DNS settings to computers and devices on a LAN. It is set up per network interface and also supports vendor options and PXE network boot. Version 1.0.3-0052 fixes several security issues (CVE-2026-2291 and CVE-2026-4890 to CVE-2026-4893).\",\"Engineering: give out addresses on a separate training-centre or test network for PLCs, HMIs and laptops, kept apart from the office LAN.\nIT: use PXE to boot new office PCs from the network when installing or reimaging them.\nIT: provide addresses for a small network whose router cannot act as a DHCP server.\",\"Confirm that no other DHCP server (usually the router or firewall) is active on the network you plan to serve.\nGive the NAS network interface a fixed IP address in Control Panel > Network > Network Interface.\nGo to Main Menu > Package Center, search for DHCP Server and click Install.\nOpen DHCP Server, go to Network Interface, select the interface and click Edit.\nTick Enable DHCP server, enter the DNS servers, lease time and the address range with subnet mask and gateway, then save.\nUse the Vendor and PXE sections only if devices need vendor options or network boot.\nCheck the list of DHCP clients to confirm devices are receiving addresses.\",\"Only one DHCP server should run on each network; two can give devices wrong addresses and break office connections.\nThe NAS must keep a fixed IP address while it acts as the DHCP server.\nPXE boot also needs a TFTP server holding the boot files, which DSM provides under Control Panel > File Services.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"dns-server, synology-directory-server, radius-server\",,\"dhcp, ip address, network, pxe, network boot, ip assignment, router, lan\",,1.0.3-0052,\ndns-server,DNS Server,icons/dns-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Utilities, Management\",,IT approval needed,\"Once staff PCs use it, a DNS fault stops name lookups for the whole office.\",IT admin,it,\"Runs the office's own DNS, so computers find the NAS and servers by name instead of IP address.\",\"DNS Server, based on BIND 9.16.34, lets the NAS translate names into IP addresses, and back, for the local network. It can host several zones, forward other lookups to internet DNS servers and use views to give different answers to different clients. Synology Directory Server depends on it; this version requires DSM 7.2 or later.\",\"Sales: open the NAS and internal web tools by an easy name instead of remembering an IP address.\nEngineering: give fixed names to test servers, HMIs and lab equipment in the training centre, so demos do not depend on IP addresses.\nSWE: point internal names at test and staging web apps hosted on the NAS.\nIT: provide the DNS zone that Synology Directory Server needs to run a Windows domain.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for DNS Server and click Install.\nOpen DNS Server, go to Zones and click Create > Master Zone, then enter the internal domain name.\nSelect the zone, click Edit > Resource Record and add A records for the NAS and other internal servers.\nGo to Resolution, tick Enable resolution services and enable forwarders, entering the ISP or public DNS servers for internet names.\nTest from a PC by running nslookup against the NAS IP address.\nWhen tests pass, set the router or DHCP server to give out the NAS as the DNS server.\",\"If staff PCs use the NAS for DNS and it goes down, they also lose internet name lookups; keep a second DNS server configured.\nAvoid .local as the internal domain name; it can conflict with Apple devices and printer discovery.\nSynology Directory Server installs and uses this package; do not remove it while the domain is in use.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"synology-directory-server, dhcp-server, ldap-server, web-station\",,\"dns, domain name, name server, hostname, zone, nslookup, internal name, ip lookup\",,9.16.34-6205,\ndocument-viewer,Document Viewer,icons/document-viewer.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,IT approval needed,Runs on Container Manager and adds memory use; Universal Viewer and Synology Office may already cover most needs.,End user,\"sales, marketing, management, engineering\",\"View Word, Excel, PowerPoint and OpenDocument files in the browser and share protected links.\",\"Document Viewer opens Microsoft Office and OpenOffice documents stored on the NAS in the browser, without downloading them or needing Office installed. Documents can be shared through an encryptable link with a validity period, a password or DSM login, and an option to block download and printing. It depends on Container Manager.\",\"Sales: share a tender document or price schedule as a view-only link that cannot be downloaded or printed and expires after the closing date.\nManagement: read reports and board papers on any computer without installing Microsoft Office.\nEngineering: open older .doc and .xls datasheets and manuals stored on the NAS straight from Synology Drive.\",\"Ask IT to review and install Document Viewer from Package Center; it depends on Container Manager.\nOpen Main Menu > Document Viewer, click Open (the folder icon), choose the document and click Select.\nOr, in Synology Drive, preview a Word, Excel or PowerPoint file and choose View > Open in Document Viewer.\nUse Zoom, Rotate, Show Thumbnails and Outlines on the toolbar to move around the document.\nTo share, click More > Share, set a Validity period, tick Enable secure sharing to require a DSM login or password, and tick Disable document download if needed.\",\"Some formats, such as .rtf, .docm, .xlsm and Visio files, only display partly.\nBlocking download also blocks printing, but readers can still take screenshots.\nIt runs through Container Manager and uses extra RAM and CPU; IT should check NAS memory before installing.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal\",\"universal-viewer, pdf-viewer, synology-office, synology-drive-server, container-manager\",container-manager,\"view word, open excel, document preview, docx viewer, read only share, view document, pptx viewer, no office installed\",,1.5.0-1306,\ndownload-station,Download Station,icons/download-station.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Productivity,,Not recommended,\"Peer-to-peer downloads bring copyright, malware and bandwidth risks, and it depends on end-of-life Python2.\",IT admin,it,\"Downloads web, FTP and torrent files directly to the NAS; not recommended at KLAE.\",\"Download Station lets the NAS download files by itself from HTTP, FTP, BitTorrent, NZB and eMule sources and from RSS feeds, so no computer needs to stay on. It can unzip finished downloads automatically and search for torrents. Synology's own description warns users to have authorisation before downloading copyrighted material.\",\"IT: download a large firmware or software image overnight directly to the NAS without leaving a PC on.\nEngineering: large configuration software installers from principals can be downloaded once by IT to a shared folder and installed from there.\nManagement: keeping BitTorrent off company equipment avoids copyright complaints against KLAE's internet line.\",\"Install only after IT and management agree on a real need; it is not recommended at KLAE.\nInstall it from Package Center (it also installs the Python2 package it depends on) and choose a destination shared folder for downloads.\nOpen Main Menu > Download Station, create a new download task and paste the download URL.\nIn its settings, turn off BitTorrent, eMule, RSS feeds and BT search if they are not needed, and set speed limits or a schedule outside office hours.\nScan downloaded files with antivirus before sharing them with staff.\",\"It depends on Python2, which is end-of-life and no longer gets security fixes.\nNever download pirated software or media; Synology itself says you need authorisation before downloading copyrighted material.\nLarge downloads compete with VPN, email and cloud backup traffic on the office internet line.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"python2, antivirus-essential, file-station, synology-drive-server\",python2,\"download, torrent, bittorrent, download manager, large file, iso, firmware download, nzb, emule\",,4.1.2-5012,\ndsm-agent,DSM Agent,icons/dsm-agent.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Productivity\",,IT approval needed,\"New 1.0 release; IT must review its terms of service, and questions may be processed by a cloud AI service.\",IT admin,it,AI assistant in DSM that answers NAS questions with guidance from Synology's official documentation.,\"DSM Agent is an assistant from Synology Inc. that answers questions about the NAS in plain language, with explanations and guidance based on Synology's official documentation. IT staff can use it to find the right DSM setting or troubleshooting steps, optionally using the DSM window open on screen as context. Version 1.0.1-0012 is listed in the regular Package Center.\",\"IT: ask how to set up a feature or clear a warning, such as a failed backup task, and get steps for our DSM version.\nIT: help a less experienced colleague at a regional office follow DSM procedures when the main administrator is away.\nManagement: quicker fixes to NAS problems mean less downtime for file sharing and email across all offices.\",\"Read DSM Agent's terms of service and Synology's privacy information, and agree with management what may be sent to a cloud AI service.\nInstall DSM Agent from Package Center with an administrator account.\nOpen DSM Agent and ask a question in plain language, for example how to set up a backup task or what a storage warning means.\nTurn on on-screen awareness only when you want it to use the open DSM window as context.\nCheck each answer against the Synology Knowledge Center before changing settings, and make changes outside office hours.\",\"It is a new 1.0 release; keep it updated in Package Center, as early versions are still being fixed.\nNever type passwords, licence keys or customer data into the chat.\nAnswers are based on Synology's documentation and can be generic; it does not replace Synology technical support.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"synology-ai-console, log-center, active-insight, storage-manager\",,\"ai assistant, chatbot, dsm help, troubleshoot, copilot, ask ai, nas support, dsm agent\",,1.0.1-0012,\nfile-station,File Station,icons/file-station.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Approved,Part of DSM and available to every staff account.,End user,all,\"Browse, search, upload, download and share NAS files from your web browser.\",\"File Station is the built-in file manager in DSM. It lets you open, search, upload, download and organise files and folders on the NAS from a web browser, and preview many file types without downloading them. You can also share files with people outside KLAE by sending a link instead of a large email attachment.\",\"Sales: search the department shared folder for an old quotation or a principal's price list from any PC, without mapping a network drive.\nMarketing: send a large product video or catalogue to an exhibition organiser as a password-protected link with an end date.\nEngineering: upload commissioning photos and test reports from a customer site or regional office through the browser.\nFinance: preview a supplier invoice PDF or a Synology Office spreadsheet in the browser before downloading it.\",\"Sign in to DSM with your NAS account and open Main Menu > File Station.\nThe left panel lists the shared folders you have permission to open. Click a folder to see its contents.\nTo find a file, type a name in the search box at the top right of the File Station window. Use the advanced search options to filter by file type, size or date.\nTo upload, drag files from your PC into the open folder, or click Upload. To download, select one or more files, right-click and choose Download (several files download as one zip file).\nDouble-click a file to preview it in the browser. Images, PDFs and Synology Office files open without downloading.\nTo share with someone outside KLAE, right-click the file or folder and choose Share. In the sharing window, set a password and an end date before you copy the link.\",\"Always protect links for customers or suppliers with a password and an end date. You can review and delete your links in Tools > Shared Links Manager.\nDeleted files can only be recovered if IT has turned on the Recycle Bin for that shared folder. Tell IT quickly if you delete something by mistake.\nFor files you edit every day or need offline on your laptop, use Synology Drive instead, which keeps version history.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"synology-drive-server, universal-search, universal-viewer, synology-office, smb-service, quickconnect\",,\"file manager, browse files, shared folder, upload, download, share link, explorer, find file, folders\",,1.4.4-2221,\nglacier-backup,Glacier Backup,icons/glacier-backup.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Backup, Business\",,Not recommended,\"Amazon no longer accepts new Glacier customers, so KLAE cannot start using it; use Hyper Backup instead.\",IT admin,it,\"Backs up NAS folders to Amazon Glacier, a legacy AWS archive service closed to new customers since Dec 2025.\",\"Glacier Backup sends copies of shared folders to Amazon Glacier in the company's own AWS account for long-term archiving, with AWS storage and retrieval charges. Amazon stopped accepting new customers for this original vault-based Glacier service on 15 December 2025, and retrieving data can take hours. Updating the package to version 1.5.2 also installs PHP 8.0 automatically.\",\"IT: none for new set-ups; send offsite copies to Synology C2 Storage or another NAS with Hyper Backup instead.\nFinance: keep archives of closed financial years with Hyper Backup, which restores much faster.\nEngineering: archive completed project files with Hyper Backup or Synology Tiering rather than a closed AWS service.\",\"Do not set up new Glacier Backup tasks; Amazon no longer accepts new Glacier accounts.\nFor offsite archives, install Hyper Backup from Main Menu > Package Center instead.\nIn Hyper Backup, choose Synology C2 Storage or a remote Synology NAS as the destination.\nIf an old Glacier Backup task is ever found, restore its data to the NAS, check it, then retire the task and the AWS vault.\",\"Amazon charges for every retrieval and retrievals can take hours.\nAmazon Glacier Deep Archive is not supported by this package.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"hyper-backup, cloud-sync, hyper-backup-vault\",,\"amazon glacier, aws backup, archive, cold storage, cloud archive, long term backup\",,1.5.2-1405,\nhybrid-share,Hybrid Share,icons/hybrid-share.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Business,,IT approval needed,\"Each Hybrid Share folder adds to the paid C2 subscription, so only IT creates them.\",IT admin,it,\"Shared folders kept in Synology C2 cloud with a fast local cache on the NAS, shareable across offices.\",\"Hybrid Share keeps the full contents of selected shared folders in Synology C2 Storage while the NAS holds a local cache of recently used files for fast access. Staff use these folders like any other shared folder, and the same folder can be mounted on up to 10 Synology NAS at different sites for cross-site work, with end-to-end AES-256 encryption. It needs a paid C2 subscription, now called the OneStorage plan.\",\"Sales: give HQ and any regional office with its own Synology NAS the same folder of price lists and quotation templates.\nEngineering: keep large project and drawing archives in C2 without filling the NAS disks, while recent projects open quickly from the local cache.\nManagement: get key folders back quickly after a NAS failure or disaster, because the full data is already held in C2.\nIT: avoid buying larger disks for folders that are mostly old files.\",\"Open Main Menu > Hybrid Share and link it to the company Synology Account that holds the C2 subscription.\nReview the Hybrid Share folders, their local cache and the C2 storage used.\nTo add a folder, go to Control Panel > Shared Folder and mount a Hybrid Share folder or convert an existing shared folder.\nKeep the C2 Encryption Key in a safe place outside the NAS.\nSet user and group permissions in Control Panel > Shared Folder, the same as for normal folders.\nTo share a folder with another office, mount the same Hybrid Share folder on that office's Synology NAS.\",\"Files not in the local cache are downloaded from C2 when opened, so they open more slowly and need a working internet link.\nWithout the Synology Account and C2 Encryption Key the data cannot be accessed; store the key safely.\nHybrid Share folders cannot be added to Synology Tiering plans.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Network drive, Background service\",\"cloud-sync, hyper-backup, file-station, smb-service, storage-manager\",,\"c2, cloud folder, hybrid cloud, multi site, branch office, cache, onestorage, share between offices\",,1.5.2-1832,\nhyper-backup,Hyper Backup,icons/hyper-backup.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Backup, Business\",,Approved,Strongly recommended: it is the main way to keep an offsite copy of company files.,IT admin,it,\"Makes versioned, encrypted backups of NAS folders, apps and LUNs to C2 cloud, another NAS or a USB drive.\",\"Hyper Backup copies shared folders, package data, system settings and LUNs from the NAS to other destinations: Synology C2 Storage, a second Synology NAS, a USB drive or public cloud storage. It keeps multiple deduplicated versions with rotation rules, can encrypt backups, and lets IT browse versions in Backup Explorer to restore files.\",\"Finance: keep nightly offsite versions of accounting and payroll folders, so a fire, theft or ransomware attack at HQ does not destroy the only copy.\nSales: restore last week's version of the quotation and price list folders if files are overwritten or encrypted.\nEngineering: keep long-term versions of project, commissioning and as-built documents that customers may ask for years later.\nIT: send an encrypted copy to Synology C2 or a NAS at a regional office to follow the 3-2-1 backup rule.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Hyper Backup and click Install (it needs DSM 7.3 or later).\nOpen Hyper Backup, click + and choose Data backup task.\nPick a destination: Synology C2 Storage, a remote Synology NAS, a local USB drive or a supported cloud service.\nSelect the shared folders and applications to back up.\nTurn on client-side encryption, backup integrity check and a rotation policy such as Smart Recycle, then set a nightly schedule.\nRun the first backup, then test a restore by browsing versions in Backup Explorer.\",\"Follow the 3-2-1 rule: three copies of data, on two types of storage, with one offsite.\nStore the encryption password and key file outside the NAS; without them the backup cannot be restored.\nTest a restore at least every quarter; a backup that has never been restored is not proven.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Desktop app, Background service\",\"hyper-backup-vault, snapshot-replication, usb-copy, active-backup-for-business, cloud-sync\",,\"backup, offsite backup, restore, c2 backup, usb backup, cloud backup, disaster recovery, 3-2-1, versions\",,4.2.2-4262,\nhyper-backup-vault,Hyper Backup Vault,icons/hyper-backup-vault.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Backup, Business\",,IT approval needed,Only useful with a second Synology NAS; install it on the NAS that receives the backups.,IT admin,it,Lets this NAS receive and store Hyper Backup copies sent from another Synology NAS.,\"Hyper Backup Vault is installed on the Synology NAS that receives backups. It lets other Synology NAS back up to it with Hyper Backup and shows an overview of all backup targets stored on it, with their logs and space used. It is useful when one office keeps the backups of another office's NAS.\",\"IT: keep an offsite backup of the Puchong HQ NAS on a NAS at a regional office, and the reverse.\nManagement: keep backup copies on hardware KLAE owns, without monthly cloud storage fees.\nFinance: have a second site hold copies of accounting folders, so a disaster at HQ does not stop month-end closing.\",\"On the receiving NAS (DSM 7.3 or later), go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Hyper Backup Vault and click Install.\nCreate a shared folder for incoming backups and a DSM account with permission to it for the sending NAS to use.\nAllow the Hyper Backup Vault port (TCP 6281) between the two sites, preferably over a site-to-site VPN rather than the open internet.\nOn the sending NAS, create a Hyper Backup task with a remote Synology NAS as the destination and enter the receiving NAS address and account.\nOpen Hyper Backup Vault on the receiving NAS to check the backup targets, logs and storage used.\",\"Place the receiving NAS in a different building or office from the source; a backup in the same room is not offsite.\nUse a dedicated backup account and keep Hyper Backup client-side encryption on.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"hyper-backup, active-backup-for-business-agent, snapshot-replication, vpn-server\",,\"backup destination, remote backup, offsite backup, backup server, receive backups, vault\",,4.2.2-4262,\nldap-server,LDAP Server,icons/ldap-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Utilities, Management\",,IT approval needed,Changes how staff accounts are managed; decide between it and Synology Directory Server first.,IT admin,it,Holds one central set of staff accounts and groups that the NAS and other systems use for sign-in.,\"LDAP Server turns the NAS into a central directory of user accounts and groups for access control, authentication and account management. Other Synology NAS and LDAP-aware applications can use it to check sign-ins, so each person has one account. It can act as a provider server or as a consumer of another Synology LDAP Server, and includes backup and restore, user import and Google Workspace (G Suite) single sign-on.\",\"HR: when a staff member joins or leaves, create or disable one account and their access to every connected NAS changes at once.\nIT: let the NAS at each regional office use the same staff accounts as Puchong HQ by joining them to the HQ LDAP server.\nIT: use LDAP users in RADIUS Server so staff sign in to office Wi-Fi with their own account.\nSWE: let internal web apps check staff sign-ins against LDAP instead of keeping separate passwords.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for LDAP Server and click Install.\nOpen LDAP Server, go to Settings and tick Enable LDAP Server.\nChoose As the Provider server, enter the FQDN (the internal domain name) and an administrator password, then click Apply.\nNote the Base DN and Bind DN shown in Settings; other systems need them to connect.\nCreate groups in Manage Groups and staff accounts in Manage Users, or import users from a file.\nOn other Synology NAS, join the directory in Control Panel > Domain/LDAP.\nUse Backup and Restore to export the LDAP configuration regularly.\",\"Windows PCs cannot join a plain LDAP directory; if staff PCs should sign in with company accounts, use Synology Directory Server instead.\nKeep the LDAP administrator password in a safe place; it controls every staff account.\nA regional office NAS can be set up as a consumer server that keeps a copy of the HQ directory.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"synology-directory-server, radius-server, sso-server, c2-identity-edge-server\",,\"ldap, user accounts, directory, login, staff accounts, single account, groups, authentication\",,2.4.59-2831,\nlog-center,Log Center,icons/log-center.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Utilities, Management\",,Approved,Free Synology tool that helps IT investigate problems and security events.,IT admin,it,\"Collects logs from the NAS and network devices in one place, with search, alerts and archiving.\",\"Log Center gathers and displays log messages from the NAS and from other network devices such as firewalls, switches and other NAS. IT can search and filter logs, set notifications for important events, archive old logs, and send or receive logs over the network for centralised log management.\",\"IT: collect logs from the office firewall, switches and regional office NAS in one place, so problems can be traced from HQ.\nFinance: help trace who changed, moved or deleted files in accounting folders, when file transfer logging is turned on.\nManagement: keep an archive of security and access logs for audits and incident reviews.\nIT: get an email alert when repeated failed sign-ins or other critical events appear.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Log Center and click Install.\nOpen Log Center; Overview shows recent activity, and Logs lets you search and filter entries by date, level and keyword.\nGo to Notifications and set rules to get an email when chosen events appear.\nIn Archive Settings, choose a shared folder and when old logs are archived.\nTo collect logs from other devices, create a rule in Log Receiving, then point the firewall, switch or other NAS to this NAS's IP address.\nTo copy this NAS's logs to another log server, set it up in Log Sending.\",\"Set up email in Control Panel > Notification first, or Log Center cannot send alerts.\nReceived logs can grow quickly; set archive rules and keep them on a volume with free space.\nOnly accept logs from devices you trust, and limit the receiving port in the firewall.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"storage-analyzer, active-insight, antivirus-essential, radius-server\",,\"logs, log, syslog, audit, event log, who deleted, history, alerts\",,1.3.2-2074,\nmedia-server,Media Server,icons/media-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Multimedia,,IT approval needed,\"Shares media with DLNA devices on the network without a login, so IT must review it first.\",IT admin,\"it, marketing\",\"Streams NAS music, photos and videos to TVs and stereo systems on the office network (DLNA/UPnP).\",\"Media Server streams music, photos and videos from the NAS to DLNA/UPnP devices on the same local network, such as smart TVs and stereo systems. Those devices browse and play the files without signing in to DSM. It runs in the background; staff use it only through the TV or player.\",\"Marketing: play product and company videos on a smart TV in the Puchong reception or showroom straight from the NAS.\nEngineering: show training videos on the training centre TV without carrying USB drives.\nIT: keep one central copy of display videos instead of separate USB sticks at each office.\",\"Get approval, then install Media Server from Package Center.\nPut display videos in a dedicated media folder that holds nothing confidential, and make sure it is indexed under Control Panel > Indexing Service.\nOpen Main Menu > Media Server and review General Settings, Browsing Settings and DMA Compatibility. Use DMA Compatibility to check which devices can see the media and block any that should not.\nOn the TV, open its media player or DLNA source and select the NAS.\nUse a common format such as MP4 (H.264), because since AME 4.0 the NAS does not convert video for the TV.\",\"DLNA has no password, so never index folders that contain confidential files.\nKeep it on the office network only; it must not be exposed to the internet.\",\"Background service, DSM web (Main Menu)\",\"advanced-media-extensions, audio-station, synology-photos, file-station\",,\"dlna, upnp, smart tv, play video on tv, media streaming, tv display, showroom screen\",,2.2.2-3412,\nmigration-assistant,Migration Assistant,icons/migration-assistant.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,IT approval needed,One-off tool used only when IT replaces the NAS with a supported new model.,IT admin,it,\"Moves data, packages and settings from an old Synology NAS to a new one while staff keep working.\",\"Migration Assistant is installed on a new (destination) Synology NAS to copy data, packages and system configuration from an older Synology NAS. Services stay available on the old NAS during the copy, and changes made meanwhile are synced before a short final switch-over. It is a one-off IT tool for replacing a NAS.\",\"IT: move from the current NAS to a larger model without rebuilding users, permissions and shared folders by hand.\nSales: keep working on quotations during most of the migration, with only a short break at the final switch-over.\nManagement: keep a NAS replacement project to one short planned outage instead of a weekend shutdown.\",\"Check on Synology's website that both models are supported; the new NAS needs DSM 7.3 or later.\nOn the new NAS, create a storage pool equal to or larger than the old NAS's pool.\nOn the new NAS, go to Main Menu > Package Center and install Migration Assistant (version 1.1.1-1515 or later).\nOpen Migration Assistant and follow the wizard to connect to the old NAS and start the copy.\nLet staff keep working on the old NAS while data copies, then schedule the final switch-over after office hours.\nAfter the switch-over, check shared folders, permissions, packages and licences on the new NAS before retiring the old one.\",\"All data and settings on the destination NAS are erased and replaced with those from the old NAS.\nLicences, such as Surveillance Station camera licences, are not migrated and must be moved separately.\nUse version 1.1.1-1515 or later, which fixes CVE-2026-88758.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"hyper-backup, active-backup-for-business-agent, storage-manager, surveillance-station\",,\"migrate nas, new nas, replace nas, upgrade nas, move data, transfer settings\",,1.1.1-1515,\nnote-station,Note Station,icons/note-station.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Productivity,,Approved,\"Free Synology package; fine for working notes, but final documents belong in Synology Drive.\",End user,\"engineering, sales, management, swe\",\"Notebooks for meeting notes, to-do lists and web clippings, stored on the NAS.\",\"Note Station is a note-taking app similar to Evernote or OneNote, with notes kept on the NAS. Notes support rich text, embedded media and attachments, and can be grouped in notebooks with tags, encrypted, and shared with colleagues. It also has a to-do list, a web clipper browser extension, a desktop client and a mobile app.\",\"Engineering: a shared troubleshooting notebook of known faults and fixes for HMIs, isolators and surge protectors.\nSales: record customer visit notes and follow-up to-dos in a notebook shared with the product specialist.\nManagement: keep meeting minutes and action lists in one notebook per regional office.\nSWE: clip vendor documentation pages and keep API notes with the web clipper.\",\"IT installs Note Station from Package Center.\nOpen it from Main Menu > Note Station in DSM.\nCreate a notebook (for example Customer Visits) and add notes to it. You can insert tables, images and attached files.\nAdd tags such as a customer or product name, and use the to-do list for follow-up actions, so you can find them later.\nShare a note or a whole notebook with colleagues who need to read or edit it.\nTo work outside the browser, install Note Station Client on Windows or macOS, or the DS note app on your phone.\",\"Notes are not ordinary files in Synology Drive; keep final reports and quotations in Drive.\nIf you encrypt a note with a password and forget it, the note cannot be recovered.\nInstalling Note Station also installs PHP 8.2, whose security support ends on 31 Dec 2026; IT should watch for a Synology update that moves it to a newer PHP.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Desktop app, Mobile app\",\"synology-drive-server, synology-office, synology-chat-server, synology-calendar, php-8-2\",php-8-2,\"notes, notebook, evernote, onenote, to-do, checklist, meeting minutes, web clipper, memo\",,2.6.10-3938,\noauth-service,OAuth Service,icons/oauth-service.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Approved,IT registers and reviews every connected app.,IT admin,\"it, swe\",Lets approved third-party apps use NAS resources through OAuth 2.0 instead of staff passwords.,\"OAuth Service adds OAuth 2.0 to the NAS, so resource owners can authorise third-party apps to access NAS resources without sharing their passwords. IT registers each app, sees which items users have authorised, and reviews the log. The latest version adds OAuth 2.0 Dynamic Client Registration.\",\"SWE: let an internal tool, such as a quotation or service-job tracker, reach files on the NAS through OAuth instead of storing a staff password in its code.\nIT: see in one place which apps staff have authorised, and remove access when an app is retired or a staff member leaves.\nManagement: approve integrations knowing each app only gets the access a user granted, and that access can be withdrawn without changing passwords.\",\"Open Main Menu > OAuth Service.\nOn the Application tab, register each app that needs access to the NAS, and share its client credentials only with the developer or vendor.\nOn the Authorized Item tab, review which users have authorised which apps, and remove items that are no longer needed.\nOn the Log tab, check authorisation events regularly for apps or users you do not expect.\nInclude a check of Authorized Item in the staff exit checklist.\",\"With Dynamic Client Registration, apps can register themselves, so check the Application list regularly for entries you do not recognise.\nTreat client secrets like passwords. Never put them in shared folders or emails.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"sso-server, secure-signin-service, synology-directory-server, ldap-server, web-station\",,\"oauth, api access, third-party app, app authorisation, token, integration, connect app, client id\",,1.3.0-0220,\npdf-viewer,PDF Viewer,icons/pdf-viewer.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Approved,\"Free and light Synology package; IT installs it. Drive already previews PDFs, so it is mainly for controlled sharing.\",End user,\"sales, marketing, engineering, management\",\"Open, search and print PDFs on the NAS in the browser, and share them as protected links.\",\"PDF Viewer displays PDF files stored on the NAS in the browser, with thumbnails, outlines, keyword search, attachments and printing. Its main strength is sharing: a PDF link can have a start and stop time, a limit on the number of views, a password or DSM login, and an option to block download and printing.\",\"Sales: share a priced proposal PDF through a link that stops working after the tender closing date and cannot be downloaded.\nMarketing: share a new catalogue PDF with a limited number of views before the public launch.\nEngineering: search a long product manual or hazardous-area certificate for a keyword from any PC.\",\"IT installs PDF Viewer from Package Center.\nOpen Main Menu > PDF Viewer, click Open (the folder icon), choose the PDF and click Select.\nClick Search (the magnifying glass) to find words, or use Show Thumbnails and Outlines to jump between pages.\nClick Print to print, or More > Download to save a copy.\nTo share, click More > Share, set the Validity period, tick Enable secure sharing for a password or DSM login, and tick Disable document download if the reader should not keep a copy. Then copy the link or QR code.\nEdit or delete links later under More > Settings > Manage Shared Links.\",\"Disable document download also stops the recipient from printing.\nDelete links when a tender or project closes; deleted links stop working at once.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"document-viewer, universal-viewer, synology-drive-server, file-station\",,\"pdf, pdf reader, open pdf, acrobat, share pdf, view pdf, print pdf, manual\",,,\npresto-file-server,Presto File Server,icons/presto-file-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Utilities, Productivity\",,IT approval needed,\"It needs a paid licence, so test it first with the free 30-day trial.\",IT admin,\"it, engineering, marketing\",\"Fast transfer of large files over long distances between a PC and the NAS, or between two NAS. Licence needed.\",\"Presto File Server speeds up file transfers over the internet (WAN) between a computer and the NAS or between two NAS, regardless of distance or latency. It shows connections in real time, lets IT set bandwidth limits, and supports scheduled transfers with Synology Presto Automator. It needs a paid Presto File Server licence; each NAS gets one free 30-day trial.\",\"Engineering: send large project drawings and commissioning videos between the Bintulu/Kuching office and HQ much faster than a normal upload.\nMarketing: move large product videos and exhibition photo sets between offices without waiting hours.\nIT: schedule regular transfers with Synology Presto Automator outside office hours, with bandwidth limits so daytime internet is not affected.\",\"After approval, install Presto File Server from Package Center and activate the one-time 30-day free trial.\nOpen Main Menu > Presto File Server and review the settings, including bandwidth limits and which users may connect.\nCheck which network ports Presto needs for connections from outside the office, and open only those on the router.\nHave a test user in a regional office install the Presto client on their computer, sign in with their NAS account and transfer a few large files.\nSet up Synology Presto Automator for scheduled or repeated transfers.\nUse the real-time connection monitoring to compare speeds with a normal upload before deciding to buy a licence.\",\"The free trial can be used only once per NAS, so plan a real test period before starting it.\nPresto helps with distance and latency, not with a slow internet line. Both ends still need decent bandwidth.\nFor everyday small files, Synology Drive is enough.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Desktop app\",\"synology-drive-server, vpn-server, quickconnect, hyper-backup, snapshot-replication\",,\"large file transfer, fast transfer, send big files, file transfer, slow upload, video transfer, wan acceleration, presto\",,2.1.3-1673,\nproxy-server,Proxy Server,icons/proxy-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Utilities, Management\",,IT approval needed,\"If it is installed but not used, IT should stop it.\",IT admin,it,\"Caching web proxy that can block restricted websites; if it is installed but not used, stop it.\",\"Proxy Server makes the NAS act as a caching proxy for HTTP-based services. PCs set to use it send their web traffic through the NAS, which can cache pages, keep logs and deny users access to restricted web services. The latest version fixes many security vulnerabilities (CVEs).\",\"Engineering: limit the training centre PCs in Puchong to the websites needed for courses.\nProcurement: limit shared warehouse PCs to the stock, supplier and courier websites staff need.\nIT: if no PC uses the proxy, stop it to free NAS resources and close port 3128.\",\"Open Main Menu > Proxy Server and review the Settings tab: proxy port (3128), manager email, caching and logging.\nIf it is installed, check whether anything uses it: look at the proxy log, and check the proxy setting on a few office PCs (Windows Settings > Network & internet > Proxy).\nIf nothing uses it, open Proxy Server in Package Center and choose Stop. Uninstall it later once you are sure.\nIf it stays in use, add rules on the Access tab to deny restricted web services, and use the Authentication tab so requests are tied to named users.\nCheck the Cache tab so the cache does not take too much space on the volume.\",\"Never forward port 3128 on the router. An open proxy can be abused by outsiders.\nKeep it updated if you use it, since recent versions fix many security vulnerabilities.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"dns-server, dhcp-server, log-center, vpn-server\",,\"proxy, web filter, block website, internet access, cache, website blocking, port 3128\",,5.2.0-1204,\nquickconnect,QuickConnect,icons/quickconnect.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Security,,Approved,IT limits which services it exposes and requires 2-step sign-in.,IT admin,it,\"Lets Synology apps reach the NAS over the internet with a QuickConnect ID, without router port forwarding.\",\"QuickConnect lets client apps connect to the NAS from outside the office using a QuickConnect ID instead of an IP address, without setting up port forwarding on the router. It works with File Station, Surveillance Station, Synology Drive, Synology Photos and the Synology mobile apps. IT manages it in Control Panel > External Access > QuickConnect.\",\"Engineering: field engineers open project folders in the Synology Drive mobile app at a customer site by typing the QuickConnect ID, without a VPN.\nSales: staff in the regional offices and on the road reach the latest price lists and quotation templates in Synology Drive.\nMarketing: upload exhibition photos from a phone to Synology Photos during an event.\nIT: give remote access to selected NAS services without opening ports on the HQ router.\",\"Go to Control Panel > External Access > QuickConnect.\nCheck that Enable QuickConnect is ticked and note the QuickConnect ID. Sign in with the company's Synology Account if DSM asks for it.\nOpen the advanced settings and allow only the services staff really need from outside, such as Synology Drive and Synology Photos.\nRequire 2-step sign-in for all accounts in Control Panel > Security > Account, starting with administrators.\nGive staff the QuickConnect ID. In Synology Drive Client or the Synology mobile apps they type it as the server address and sign in with their NAS account.\nFor browser access from outside, staff go to https://quickconnect.to/ followed by the QuickConnect ID.\",\"Anyone who knows the QuickConnect ID can reach the sign-in page, so strong passwords and 2-step sign-in are essential.\nWhen a direct connection is not possible, traffic is relayed through Synology's servers and can be slow. Large regular transfers may be better over VPN Server or Presto File Server.\",Background service,\"vpn-server, secure-signin-service, synology-drive-server, synology-photos, file-station, surveillance-station\",,\"remote access, access from outside, work from site, quickconnect id, connect from home, internet access, outside office\",,1.0.10-0187,\nradius-server,RADIUS Server,icons/radius-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Utilities, Management\",,IT approval needed,Changes how everyone connects to office Wi-Fi and needs access points that support WPA2/WPA3-Enterprise.,IT admin,it,Lets staff log in to office Wi-Fi with their own account instead of one shared Wi-Fi password.,\"RADIUS Server, based on FreeRADIUS 3.0.27, provides centralised authentication, authorisation and accounting for network access, such as WPA2/WPA3-Enterprise Wi-Fi. Wi-Fi access points send sign-in requests to the NAS, which checks them against local DSM users, LDAP users or domain users. IT can manage allowed clients, keep a block list and review logs.\",\"HR: when a staff member leaves, disabling their account also stops their Wi-Fi access, with no shared password to change.\nIT: replace the shared Wi-Fi password at HQ and regional offices with personal staff sign-ins.\nEngineering: let engineers' laptops join the office Wi-Fi at any KLAE office with the same personal account.\nManagement: check the RADIUS log to see which account connected when investigating an incident.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for RADIUS Server and click Install.\nOpen RADIUS Server, go to Settings and enable the RADIUS server, keeping authentication port 1812 unless IT uses another.\nChoose which accounts can sign in: Local users, LDAP users or Domain users.\nGo to Clients and add each Wi-Fi access point or controller with its IP address and a strong shared secret.\nOn the access point, create a WPA2/WPA3-Enterprise network that uses the NAS IP address, port 1812 and the same shared secret.\nTest with one laptop and one phone, then check the Log page before rolling it out to all staff.\",\"Keep a separate guest network with its own password for visitors and trainees who have no company account.\nUse long, random shared secrets and add only trusted access points as clients.\nTo use LDAP or domain users, set up LDAP Server or Synology Directory Server and join the NAS to it first.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"ldap-server, synology-directory-server, vpn-server, log-center\",,\"radius, wifi, wi-fi login, wireless, 802.1x, wpa2 enterprise, wpa3, network login, authentication\",,3.0.27-0516,\nreplication-service,Replication Service,icons/replication-service.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Backup,,Approved,No separate set-up; it is managed through Snapshot Replication.,IT admin,it,Background service that copies snapshots to another NAS; installed automatically with Snapshot Replication.,Replication Service is a core background package that replicates snapshots from a source Synology NAS to a destination. It cannot run alone and has no window of its own; Snapshot Replication and other packages with snapshot features use it for their replication tasks. Package Center installs it automatically when a package needs it.,\"IT: provides the copying engine behind Snapshot Replication tasks that send shared folders to a second NAS.\nManagement: allows a second office to hold an up-to-date copy of key folders, which shortens recovery after a site problem.\nFinance: supports replicated copies of accounting folders, so they can be brought back quickly from another NAS.\",\"There is nothing to open: it has no user interface of its own.\nIt is installed automatically when IT installs Snapshot Replication; version 1.4.0 needs DSM 7.4 or later.\nCreate and manage replication tasks in Snapshot Replication > Replication.\nKeep it updated in Main Menu > Package Center together with Snapshot Replication.\nDo not stop or uninstall it while replication tasks are in use.\",Leave it alone unless Synology support asks; it is managed by the packages that depend on it.,Background service,\"snapshot-replication, san-manager, hyper-backup\",,\"replication, snapshot copy, copy to another nas, background service, replicate\",,1.4.0-1405,\nsan-manager,SAN Manager,icons/san-manager.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Business,,Approved,For IT server storage only.,IT admin,it,Creates iSCSI and Fibre Channel storage (LUNs) that servers and VM hosts use as their own local disks.,\"SAN Manager manages and monitors the NAS's iSCSI and Fibre Channel services, which provide block-level storage. It creates LUNs, virtual disks on the NAS that servers connect to and use like local drives, and controls which hosts may connect. It is also needed by Snapshot Replication; it is for server storage, not normal staff file sharing.\",\"SWE: give a Hyper-V or VMware host shared storage for test and build virtual machines.\nFinance: keep the accounting server's data disk on the NAS, where it can be covered by NAS snapshots and backups.\nIT: provide storage for servers without buying a separate storage array.\",\"Open Main Menu > SAN Manager.\nGo to LUN, click Create, and choose the volume, size and space allocation (thick or thin provisioning).\nCreate or map an iSCSI target and turn on CHAP authentication.\nAllow only the intended server's iSCSI initiator (IQN) to connect to the target.\nOn the server, connect to the NAS address with its iSCSI Initiator, then bring the new disk online and format it.\nProtect important LUNs with snapshots (immutable snapshots need Snapshot Replication installed) and with Hyper Backup.\",\"Never connect two servers to the same LUN unless they run a cluster file system, or the data will be corrupted.\nA LUN cannot be migrated while it has immutable snapshots.\nThin-provisioned LUNs can fail if the volume fills up; watch free space in Storage Manager.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"storage-manager, snapshot-replication, smi-s-provider, virtual-machine-manager, hyper-backup\",,\"iscsi, lun, block storage, san, server storage, vmware storage, hyper-v storage, fibre channel\",,1.0.12-0802,\nsecure-signin-service,Secure SignIn Service,icons/secure-signin-service.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Security,,Approved,IT may require 2-step sign-in for every account.,End user,all,\"Safer NAS sign-in: approve logins on your phone, use a security key, or enter a one-time code.\",\"Secure SignIn Service adds sign-in options beyond a password. You can sign in without a password by approving the request in the Synology Secure SignIn app or with a hardware security key, or use 2-step sign-in with a one-time code (OTP). IT can also turn on Adaptive MFA, which asks for extra checks when a sign-in looks unusual, and Security Advisor now separates password-only attempts from full 2-step sign-ins.\",\"Sales: approve your DSM or Synology Drive sign-in with one tap on your phone instead of typing a password on a customer's PC.\nFinance: protect accounts that can open bank, payment and invoice folders, so a stolen password alone is not enough to get in.\nEngineering: field engineers sign in from shared site laptops without leaving a saved password behind.\nIT: require 2-step sign-in for everyone, especially administrators and staff who sign in from outside through QuickConnect.\",\"Install the Synology Secure SignIn app on your phone from the App Store or Google Play.\nSign in to DSM, click the person icon at the top right of the desktop and choose Personal > Account.\nUnder Sign-in Method, choose Passwordless Sign-In, pick Approve sign-in and enter your password.\nIn the Secure SignIn app, tap + and scan the QR code shown in DSM, then finish the wizard.\nIf IT asks you to use a one-time code instead, set up 2-factor authentication on the same page and add the account to the Secure SignIn app, which then shows the codes.\nNext time you sign in, open the app and tap to approve, or type the current code.\nIf you change or lose your phone, tell IT straight away so they can reset your sign-in method.\",\"Never approve a sign-in request you did not start. Deny it and tell IT.\nApprove sign-in needs the NAS to reach Synology's push notification service. A hardware security key (USB key, Windows Hello or Touch ID) only works when you open DSM by its HTTPS domain name, not through QuickConnect or an IP address.\",\"Mobile app, DSM web (Main Menu)\",\"quickconnect, sso-server, vpn-server, oauth-service, synology-drive-server\",,\"2fa, two factor, otp, login, sign in, password, authenticator, security key, passwordless, mfa\",,1.1.7-0455,\nsmb-service,SMB Service,icons/smb-service.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Approved,This is what makes our mapped network drives work.,End user,all,\"Lets Windows, macOS and Linux PCs open NAS shared folders as network drives.\",\"SMB Service runs the SMB/CIFS file sharing protocol on the NAS. With SMB enabled in Control Panel > File Services > SMB, staff can open shared folders as network drives in Windows File Explorer, macOS Finder or Linux file browsers. Active Backup for Business and Synology Directory Server depend on it, and the latest version reconnects properly after a network interruption during a transfer.\",\"Finance: open the accounts shared folder as a drive letter in File Explorer and save spreadsheets straight from Excel.\nEngineering: keep project drawings and commissioning reports on one mapped drive so the whole project team works from the same files.\nProcurement: open stock lists and delivery orders from a mapped drive on the Puchong warehouse PCs.\nIT: keep SMB running because Active Backup for Business and Synology Directory Server depend on it.\",\"On an office Windows PC, open File Explorer, right-click This PC and choose Map network drive.\nPick a drive letter and type the folder address IT gives you, for example \\\\<nas-name>\\<shared-folder>. Tick Reconnect at sign-in.\nIf Windows asks, sign in with your NAS username and password (tick Connect using different credentials if your PC account is different).\nOn a Mac, in Finder choose Go > Connect to Server, type smb://<nas-address>/<shared-folder> and click Connect.\nOpen, save and rename files on the drive as you would on your own PC. You only see folders your account has permission to open.\nFrom outside the office, connect through the company VPN first. Network drives are not opened to the internet.\",\"Files deleted from a network drive do not go to your PC's Recycle Bin. They can only be recovered if IT turned on the shared folder's Recycle Bin or snapshots.\nIT: never forward SMB port 445 on the router, and keep the minimum SMB protocol at SMB2 or higher in Control Panel > File Services > SMB > Advanced Settings.\",\"Network drive, Background service\",\"file-station, synology-drive-server, active-backup-for-business, synology-directory-server, vpn-server, snapshot-replication\",,\"network drive, map drive, mapped drive, shared drive, z drive, smb, cifs, windows share, file server\",,4.15.13-4251,\nsmi-s-provider,SMI-S Provider,icons/smi-s-provider.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Not recommended,No business need unless IT manages Hyper-V through Microsoft SCVMM.,IT admin,it,Lets Microsoft System Center Virtual Machine Manager (SCVMM) manage NAS storage from its own console.,\"SMI-S Provider makes the NAS follow SMI-S, an industry standard that storage management software uses to talk to storage systems. With it, Microsoft System Center Virtual Machine Manager (SCVMM) can manage one or more Synology NAS as storage nodes from its own console. It is only useful where Hyper-V is managed with SCVMM.\",\"IT: only if KLAE adopts SCVMM, create and assign NAS storage to Hyper-V hosts from the SCVMM console.\nSWE: none today; test VMs can use iSCSI storage from SAN Manager directly.\nIT: for normal iSCSI needs, use SAN Manager instead.\",\"Confirm KLAE runs Microsoft System Center Virtual Machine Manager; if not, do not install this package.\nGo to Main Menu > Package Center, search for SMI-S Provider and click Install (it needs DSM 7.2 or later).\nOpen the package and enable the SMI-S service.\nIn SCVMM, add the NAS as an SMI-S storage provider using the NAS address and an administrator account.\nCreate and assign storage to Hyper-V hosts from the SCVMM console.\",It exposes storage management over the network; leave it uninstalled unless SCVMM is in use.,Background service,\"san-manager, storage-manager, virtual-machine-manager\",,\"smi-s, scvmm, system center, hyper-v, storage provider, microsoft\",,1.1.2-2018,\nsnapshot-replication,Snapshot Replication,icons/snapshot-replication.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Backup, Business\",,Approved,Recommended first line of defence against accidental deletion and ransomware.,IT admin,it,\"Takes quick, space-saving snapshots of shared folders so deleted or encrypted files can be rolled back.\",\"Snapshot Replication takes point-in-time snapshots of shared folders and LUNs on Btrfs volumes, on a schedule with retention rules, to protect against accidental deletion, application crashes, data corruption and viruses. Files can be restored from a snapshot in seconds, and immutable snapshots cannot be deleted or changed, even by an administrator, until they expire. Snapshots can also be replicated to a second Synology NAS.\",\"Sales: get yesterday's version of a quotation folder back in minutes after someone overwrites or deletes files.\nFinance: roll back the accounts shared folder to the hour before a ransomware attack encrypted it.\nEngineering: restore a project folder to how it looked before a bad bulk edit, using Previous Versions in Windows File Explorer.\nIT: replicate key shared folders to a second NAS at another office for quick recovery.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Snapshot Replication and click Install; Replication Service is installed with it, and it also needs SAN Manager.\nOpen Snapshot Replication > Snapshots, select a shared folder on a Btrfs volume and click Settings.\nSet a schedule (for example every hour during office hours) and a retention policy.\nIn the same settings, make snapshots visible so staff can restore files themselves from the #snapshot folder or Windows Previous Versions.\nTurn on immutable snapshots for critical folders such as Finance and Sales, with a protection period of, for example, 7 days.\nUse the Recovery section to restore a whole folder, and the Replication section to copy snapshots to a second Synology NAS.\nCheck the Log section regularly for failed snapshots.\",\"Snapshots live on the same disks as the data; they do not help if the NAS itself fails, so also use Hyper Backup.\nImmutable snapshots cannot be deleted early and use space until they expire.\nShared folders must be on a Btrfs volume.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Network drive, Background service\",\"replication-service, san-manager, hyper-backup, storage-manager, synology-high-availability\",\"replication-service, san-manager\",\"snapshot, previous versions, restore deleted file, undo, ransomware, rollback, immutable, recover file\",,7.5.1-1915,\nsso-server,SSO Server,icons/sso-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Utilities\",,IT approval needed,\"Needs a domain name with HTTPS and a valid certificate, and changes how staff sign in to connected apps.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",Lets staff sign in once with their NAS account to other Synology NAS and internal web apps.,\"SSO Server turns the NAS into a single sign-on identity provider. Other Synology NAS and internal web apps can send users to it to sign in with their DSM or directory account, using the OIDC or SAML standards or Synology SSO. Each app is registered as an application profile, which gives it the details it needs, such as an application ID and secret for OIDC.\",\"SWE: let internal web tools built by the team use OIDC sign-in with staff accounts instead of storing their own passwords.\nIT: let staff sign in to the NAS at each regional office through the same single sign-on page as at Puchong HQ.\nHR: when a staff member leaves, disabling one account removes their access to every app connected to single sign-on.\nSales: open the NAS and internal tools without typing a password again for each one.\",\"Make sure the NAS has a domain name reachable over HTTPS with a valid certificate (Control Panel > Security > Certificate); an IP address or QuickConnect link will not work.\nGo to Main Menu > Package Center, search for SSO Server and click Install.\nOpen SSO Server, go to Service, set the server URL and enable OIDC, SAML or both.\nChoose which accounts can sign in, such as local and directory users or directory users only.\nCreate an application profile for each app and enter its redirect URI; OIDC apps receive an application ID and secret.\nEnter the OIDC well-known URL or the SAML IdP metadata in the app; for another Synology NAS, use Control Panel > Domain/LDAP > SSO Client.\nTest sign-in with a normal staff account before rolling it out.\",\"The server URL must be a domain name with a valid TLS certificate; it does not work with an IP address or QuickConnect.\nThe SSO Server NAS and any Synology client NAS need DSM 7.2 or later.\nKeep application secrets private; anyone who has one could pretend to be that app.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal, Background service\",\"synology-directory-server, ldap-server, oauth-service, secure-signin-service\",,\"sso, single sign-on, login once, oidc, saml, openid, sign in, one password\",,,\nstorage-analyzer,Storage Analyzer,icons/storage-analyzer.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Utilities, Management\",,Approved,,IT admin,it,\"Creates reports on how NAS space is used, including the biggest, oldest and duplicate files.\",\"Storage Analyzer scans volumes and shared folders and produces reports on space use, such as the largest files, files not changed for a long time, possible duplicates and usage by owner or file type. Reports can run on a schedule and are saved for later review. It helps IT find what is filling the NAS before buying more disks.\",\"Marketing: find duplicate copies of large product videos and exhibition photos stored in several folders.\nEngineering: list old project folders not changed in years that can be archived.\nManagement: get a regular report of space used per shared folder when planning storage upgrades.\nIT: find out what suddenly filled a volume, such as a large video dump or a misplaced backup.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Storage Analyzer and click Install.\nOpen Storage Analyzer and click Create to set up a report.\nChoose the report types (for example large files, duplicate file candidates, least modified files) and the volumes or shared folders to scan.\nChoose where the report is saved and an optional schedule, such as monthly.\nRun the report and open it to review the results.\nShare the findings with department heads and agree what to archive or delete.\",\"Scanning large volumes uses CPU and disk time; schedule reports after office hours.\nReports list file names and owners, so save them in a folder only IT can open.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"storage-manager, synology-tiering-vault, file-station, hybrid-share\",,\"disk space, storage report, large files, duplicate files, what is using space, nas full, cleanup\",,,\nstorage-manager,Storage Manager,icons/storage-manager.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Productivity,,Approved,Core DSM tool; only IT administrators should use it.,IT admin,it,\"Built-in DSM tool for managing the NAS's drives, storage pools, volumes, SSD cache and drive health.\",\"Storage Manager is where IT creates and manages storage pools and volumes, adds or replaces drives, sets up SSD cache and checks drive health. It shows RAID status, free space and drive test results, and can run S.M.A.R.T. tests and data scrubbing. It is part of DSM, so there is nothing to install.\",\"IT: replace a failed drive and follow the RAID repair, so shared folders stay online while it rebuilds.\nIT: expand a volume when the Sales and Engineering shared folders are running out of space.\nFinance: avoid lost work at month-end, because IT is warned early about failing drives and full volumes.\nManagement: get clear figures on used and free space when planning NAS upgrades.\",\"Open Main Menu > Storage Manager (administrators only).\nCheck the Overview page for the health of storage pools, volumes and drives.\nIn HDD/SSD, check each drive's health status and schedule S.M.A.R.T. tests.\nIn Storage, select a storage pool to run data scrubbing, or to repair it after replacing a failed drive.\nWhen adding drives, use the Storage page to create or expand storage pools and volumes.\nSet up email alerts in Control Panel > Notification so IT hears about drive or volume problems.\",\"Deleting a volume or storage pool erases all its data; check twice before confirming.\nSnapshots, Active Backup for Business and Synology Tiering need Btrfs volumes.\nKeep a spare drive of the same type on hand to replace a failed one quickly.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"storage-analyzer, san-manager, snapshot-replication, active-insight, hyper-backup\",,\"disk, hard drive, raid, storage pool, volume, disk health, ssd cache, capacity, failed drive\",,,\nsurveillance-station,Surveillance Station,icons/surveillance-station.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Utilities\",,IT approval needed,\"Needs IP cameras, paid licences beyond two cameras and plenty of disk space, and raises privacy duties.\",IT admin,\"it, hr, procurement, management\",\"Records and monitors IP cameras for offices, warehouse and training centre; 2 free camera licences.\",\"Surveillance Station is Synology's video management system for IP cameras. It records camera footage to the NAS, shows live and recorded video, sends alerts on motion and other events, and lets authorised staff watch from a browser, the Surveillance Station Client desktop app or the DS cam mobile app. The NAS includes two free camera licences; more cameras need paid licences.\",\"Procurement: record the warehouse loading bay and stock area to check deliveries, damaged goods or missing stock.\nHR: monitor office entrances after hours and review footage after an incident.\nEngineering: watch the training centre and demo rooms where expensive demo kits are kept.\nManagement: view cameras at regional offices from the DS cam mobile app.\",\"Plan the cameras, check them against Synology's IP camera compatibility list, and work out the licences and storage needed.\nInstall Surveillance Station from Package Center and choose the volume for recordings.\nOpen Surveillance Station, go to IP Camera and click Add to find the cameras on the network and add them.\nSet each camera's recording schedule (continuous or on motion) and how many days of footage to keep.\nAdd paid camera licences in the License section when more than two cameras are needed.\nGive HR, warehouse or management users view-only access to just the cameras they need.\nHave those users install Surveillance Station Client on Windows or macOS, or the DS cam app on their phones.\",\"Recording writes to disk all day; use a separate volume or surveillance-rated drives and watch free space.\nPut up CCTV notices and limit who can view or export footage, in line with Malaysia's PDPA.\nOn NAS models outside the DVA series, install Surveillance Video Extension to play back H.264 (AVC) recordings.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Desktop app, Mobile app\",\"surveillance-video-extension, advanced-media-extensions, storage-manager, hyper-backup\",,\"cctv, camera, surveillance, security camera, nvr, video recording, ip camera, monitoring\",,,\nsurveillance-video-extension,Surveillance Video Extension,icons/surveillance-video-extension.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Security\",,IT approval needed,Only needed if Surveillance Station is used with H.264 cameras; install it together with that.,IT admin,it,Add-on that lets Surveillance Station play back H.264 (AVC) camera recordings on the NAS.,Surveillance Video Extension keeps server-side AVC (H.264) processing for Surveillance Station after Synology moved general video decoding to end devices in AME 4.0. It lets Surveillance Station play back H.264 recordings on NAS models outside the DVA series. It runs in the background and has nothing for staff to open.,\"Procurement: warehouse supervisors can play back H.264 camera footage in Surveillance Station when checking a stock discrepancy.\nHR: incident footage from office cameras can be reviewed and exported without codec problems.\nIT: keep existing H.264 cameras in use instead of replacing them.\",\"Install it only if Surveillance Station is in use and the cameras record in H.264 (AVC).\nMake sure Surveillance Station is version 9.2.1 or later, as Synology recommends.\nCheck that our NAS model is on the supported list; DVA-series models already keep AVC and HEVC support.\nInstall Surveillance Video Extension from Package Center while the NAS is connected to the internet, because it must be installed online.\nPlay back an H.264 recording in Surveillance Station to confirm it works.\",\"It has no effect unless Surveillance Station is installed.\nIt is not a general video codec; it does not help Synology Photos, Synology Drive or Media Server.\",Background service,\"surveillance-station, advanced-media-extensions\",,\"cctv playback, h.264, avc, camera codec, surveillance codec, video extension, cctv video\",,,\nsynology-ai-console,Synology AI Console,icons/synology-ai-console.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Productivity\",,IT approval needed,\"Provider fees apply and company text goes to an outside AI service, so IT controls access.\",IT admin,it,Admin tool that connects AI providers to Synology Office and MailPlus and controls who uses AI.,\"Synology AI Console lets IT connect a third-party AI service, such as OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Google Gemini, Amazon Bedrock or another OpenAI-compatible provider, to supported Synology packages including MailPlus and Synology Office. IT decides which packages and users get AI features, can mask sensitive data before it is sent, and can review usage logs. Synology does not charge for AI requests, but the AI provider does.\",\"Sales: with AI turned on in MailPlus, summarise long email threads with principals and customers and suggest follow-up actions.\nMarketing: draft, polish and proofread brochure and website text in Synology Office.\nFinance: get help finding the right spreadsheet formula in Synology Office.\nIT: limit AI to selected groups and track usage so provider costs stay predictable.\",\"Open Main Menu > AI Console in DSM with an administrator account.\nOn the Overview page, add an API integration: choose the AI provider, enter the API key from the provider's account, and apply it to the packages that should use it.\nOn the Permissions page, enable AI for MailPlus or Synology Office and choose the users or groups allowed to use it, rather than all users.\nOn the De-identification page, click Enable, choose the languages and the types of data to mask. This needs Container Manager and at least 8 GB of RAM.\nCheck the logs regularly and compare usage with the provider's bill.\nTell staff which AI features are on and what must not be sent, such as customer pricing or personal data.\",\"Set a monthly spending limit in the AI provider's account, because the provider bills per token.\nSynology says de-identification cannot guarantee that all sensitive data is masked; each language pack also uses about 1 GB of RAM.\nAI Console 2.0 (beta, June 2026) adds on-device AI models for GPU-equipped NAS models to power AI Search in Synology Drive; check whether our model qualifies.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"synology-office, synology-mailplus, synology-mailplus-server, synology-drive-server, dsm-agent, container-manager\",,\"ai, chatgpt, openai, gemini, copilot, artificial intelligence, llm, ai writing, summarise email\",,,\nsynology-application-service,Synology Application Service,icons/synology-application-service.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Approved,\"Synology Drive, Office, Photos, Chat, Contacts and MailPlus need it; keep it installed while any of them is.\",IT admin,it,\"Background service that gives Synology apps like Drive, Chat and MailPlus shared notifications and profiles.\",\"Synology Application Service is a background framework for Synology's collaboration apps. It provides shared services such as email, mobile and browser notifications, and profile settings (photo, nickname, display language) that carry across apps. Package Center lists it as a dependency of Synology Drive Server, Synology Office, Synology Photos, Synology Chat Server, Synology Contacts and Synology MailPlus.\",\"IT: keep the shared framework that Synology Drive Server, Office, Photos, Chat, Contacts and MailPlus need, so those apps keep working after updates.\nEngineering: field engineers get a mobile notification for new Chat messages or shared files while they are at a customer site.\nSales: get a browser notification when a colleague shares a revised quotation, even when the app is not open.\nManagement: set your profile photo and display language once and see it in the other Synology collaboration apps.\",\"Open Package Center > Installed and check that Synology Application Service shows Running.\nDo not stop or uninstall it. Synology Drive Server, Synology Office, Synology Photos, Synology Chat Server, Synology Contacts and Synology MailPlus all depend on it.\nInstall its updates when Package Center offers them, because newer versions of the dependent apps may need a newer version of this service.\nIf a dependent app will not start after a DSM update, check this package first in Package Center and use Repair if it is offered.\nTell staff that browser notifications only work when they open DSM through its HTTPS address.\",\"Staff never open this package directly; it works in the background.\nThis is separate from DSM system alerts, which IT sets up in Control Panel > Notification.\",Background service,\"synology-drive-server, synology-office, synology-photos, synology-chat-server, synology-contacts, synology-mailplus, synology-calendar\",,\"background service, notifications, push notification, framework, dependency, required package, profile\",,,\nsynology-calendar,Synology Calendar,icons/synology-calendar.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Productivity,,Approved,Free Synology package; IT installs it from Package Center.,End user,\"management, sales, engineering, hr, marketing\",\"Shared web calendars for meetings, site visits, training and leave, with sync to phones.\",\"Synology Calendar is a web calendar hosted on the NAS. Staff can keep personal calendars, share calendars with colleagues or groups, invite guests to events, and sync with phone and computer calendar apps through CalDAV. It is a company-controlled alternative to personal Google or phone calendars for team schedules.\",\"Engineering: a shared field-service calendar showing which engineer is at which site for commissioning or servicing, visible to all regional offices.\nEngineering: publish the Puchong training centre course schedule so sales can tell customers which dates are still open.\nHR: a shared leave and public-holiday calendar per office, including state holidays that differ between Selangor, Penang, Terengganu, Johor and Sarawak.\nSales: plan customer visits, exhibitions and principal meetings on a team calendar that managers can see.\",\"IT installs Synology Calendar from Package Center and gives your account access.\nOpen it from Main Menu > Calendar in DSM, or from the app launcher icon at the top of the Synology Drive web portal.\nClick a date to create an event, add the location (for example the customer's plant) and invite colleagues as guests.\nTo share a calendar with your team, open the calendar's menu in the left panel, add the users or groups, and choose whether they can only view or also edit.\nTo see it on your phone, open Package settings > CalDAV Account in Synology Calendar and copy the CalDAV URL. On iPhone, add it as an Other > CalDAV account in the Calendar settings; on Android, use an app such as DAVx5.\nUse the same CalDAV address in Thunderbird or the macOS Calendar app to see your events on a computer.\",\"CalDAV sync does not work through QuickConnect; ask IT for the correct NAS address or VPN for phone sync.\nMicrosoft Outlook has no built-in CalDAV support, so Outlook users need an add-on approved by IT.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal\",\"synology-contacts, synology-mailplus, synology-chat-server, synology-drive-server\",,\"calendar, schedule, meeting, appointment, leave calendar, caldav, booking, events, shared calendar, roster\",,,\nsynology-chat-server,Synology Chat Server,icons/synology-chat-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Productivity,,IT approval needed,\"Free Synology app, but it installs the end-of-life Node.js v18 runtime and a newer ChatPlus Server is in beta, so IT should decide before rollout.\",End user,all,\"Private team chat with channels, direct messages and file sharing, hosted on the NAS.\",\"Synology Chat Server provides web-based real-time chat for staff, similar to Slack or Teams chat, with all messages kept on the NAS. It supports public and private channels, one-to-one chats, file and image sharing, and desktop and mobile apps with notifications. Developers can also post automatic messages into channels with webhooks and bots.\",\"Engineering: a field-service channel where engineers on site post photos of panel wiring and get quick help from product specialists in Puchong.\nSales: a private channel per key account or tender to discuss pricing, kept off personal WhatsApp groups.\nProcurement: a warehouse channel announcing stock arrivals so sales can confirm delivery dates to customers.\nSWE: send build results or server alerts into a channel through an incoming webhook.\",\"After approval, IT installs Synology Chat Server from Package Center. Your NAS account is then your chat account.\nOpen it from Main Menu > Chat in DSM, or from the app launcher in the Synology Drive web portal.\nInstall the Synology Chat desktop app (Windows or macOS) and the Synology Chat mobile app (iOS or Android), and sign in with the NAS address and your NAS account.\nJoin the channels for your team, or create a new channel and make it private if only invited people should see it.\nStart a direct message by clicking a colleague's name. Drag a file into the conversation to share it.\nType @ and a colleague's name to get their attention; they receive a notification.\",\"Installing it also installs Node.js v18, which reached end-of-life on 30 Apr 2025; IT should note this and watch for a Synology update that moves to a newer Node.js.\nSynology started a beta of a newer ChatPlus Server in August 2026; IT should check Synology's plans before rolling Chat Server out company-wide.\nPhones outside the office can only connect if IT has set up remote access such as QuickConnect or VPN.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal, Desktop app, Mobile app\",\"synology-drive-server, synology-calendar, synology-mailplus, quickconnect, synology-office, nodejs-v18\",\"nodejs-v18, synology-application-service\",\"chat, messaging, instant message, slack, teams, whatsapp, group chat, channel, message colleague\",,2.4.7-22203,\nsynology-contacts,Synology Contacts,icons/synology-contacts.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Productivity, Management\",,Approved,Free Synology package; IT installs it from Package Center.,End user,\"sales, procurement, engineering, marketing, management\",\"Shared company address books for customers and suppliers, with sync to phones.\",\"Synology Contacts keeps personal and shared company address books on the NAS. Staff can import contacts from Google or Outlook, migrate contacts from Synology MailPlus, organise them with labels, share address books with colleagues by permission level, and sync them to iPhones and other devices through CardDAV. Synology MailPlus webmail depends on it.\",\"Sales: a shared address book of customer buyers, plant engineers and consultants, so contacts stay with KLAE when a salesperson leaves.\nProcurement: one address book of principals, forwarders and suppliers used by every office.\nEngineering: field engineers sync site contacts such as plant supervisors and safety officers to their phones before a commissioning visit.\nMarketing: keep exhibition leads in a separate address book before handing them over to sales.\",\"IT installs Synology Contacts from Package Center.\nOpen it from Main Menu > Contacts in DSM.\nTo bring in existing contacts, click + next to Personal Address Book, choose Import Address Book, then pick the file you exported from Google or Outlook, or a vCard (.vcf) file.\nAdd a new contact with the company name, phone numbers and email, and use labels or separate address books (for example Customers and Suppliers) to keep them organised.\nTo share an address book, hover over it in the left panel, open its menu and share it with the colleagues or groups who need it.\nTo get the contacts on your phone, hover over the address book, open its menu, choose CardDAV and copy the URL. On iPhone, add it as an Other > CardDAV account; on Android, use an app such as DAVx5.\",\"CardDAV sync fails on iPhone, Mac and Outlook if your NAS account name contains a space.\nImport works with Google and Outlook exports and vCard files; a contact list typed in Excel may need converting first.\nAddress books hold personal data, so share them only with staff who need them, in line with Malaysia's PDPA.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal\",\"synology-calendar, synology-mailplus, synology-mailplus-server, synology-chat-server\",\"nodejs-v22, synology-application-service\",\"contacts, address book, phone book, customer list, vcard, carddav, supplier contacts, phone numbers\",,1.0.11-20661,\nsynology-directory-server,Synology Directory Server,icons/synology-directory-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Utilities, Management\",,IT approval needed,Changes how every PC and staff member signs in; plan it carefully and back it up.,IT admin,it,\"Runs a Windows-style Active Directory domain on the NAS for company accounts, PCs and policies.\",\"Synology Directory Server provides an Active Directory domain service powered by Samba. IT can manage user accounts and groups, join Windows, Linux and Synology NAS devices to the domain, use Kerberos sign-in and apply group policies. Version 4.15.13-0657 needs SMB Service 4.15.13-4209 or later and also depends on the DNS Server package.\",\"HR: create one account for a new hire that opens their PC, the NAS and their department folders, and disable it on their last day.\nIT: apply password rules and other group policies to all domain-joined Windows PCs from one place.\nFinance: limit the accounting and payroll folders to members of the Finance group, managed centrally in the domain.\nEngineering: let engineers sign in to any domain-joined PC in the office or training centre with their own account.\",\"Give the NAS a fixed IP address in Control Panel > Network and agree the domain name with IT.\nGo to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Synology Directory Server and click Install; DNS Server and SMB Service are installed or updated as dependencies.\nOpen Synology Directory Server and complete the Domain setup with the domain name, NetBIOS name and administrator password.\nGo to Users & Computers to create organisational units, groups and staff accounts.\nUse Domain Policy to set password rules and other policies.\nSet staff PCs to use the NAS as their DNS server.\nJoin each Windows PC in Settings > System > About > Domain or workgroup, choose Domain, enter the domain name and an administrator account, then restart; check the Log page if joining fails.\",\"Only Windows Pro or Enterprise editions can join a domain; Windows Home cannot.\nThe domain controller is critical: back it up with Hyper Backup and consider a second domain controller so sign-ins keep working if this NAS is down.\nChoose one directory for the company; use this instead of LDAP Server if staff PCs should sign in with company accounts.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"dns-server, smb-service, ldap-server, radius-server, sso-server\",\"dns-server, smb-service\",\"active directory, ad, domain, domain controller, user accounts, group policy, windows login, kerberos, samba\",,4.15.13-0657,\nsynology-drive-server,Synology Drive Server,icons/synology-drive-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Productivity\",,Approved,Our main tool for storing and sharing work files.,End user,all,\"Company file sharing and sync: team folders, version history, share links, desktop and mobile apps.\",\"Synology Drive Server provides file storage, management, sharing and sync in a private cloud on the NAS, similar to Google Drive or OneDrive but on our own hardware. Teams can reach files securely from PCs and phones, share files by link, and roll back to earlier versions. It also backs up computers and hosts Synology Office documents.\",\"Sales: keep one Team Folder of principals' price lists, quotation templates and tender documents, so all five regional offices open the same latest version.\nEngineering: sync project folders to field engineers' laptops, so drawings, loop diagrams and commissioning checklists are on hand at site even without internet.\nMarketing: send brochures and catalogues to customers or exhibition organisers as a password-protected link that expires, instead of large email attachments.\nFinance: restore the earlier version of a spreadsheet that was overwritten by mistake, without asking IT.\",\"Open it in a browser: sign in to DSM and click Main Menu > Synology Drive, or go to the Drive portal address IT gives you (for example https://<nas-address>/drive).\nFind your files in the left panel: My Drive is your own space, Team Folder holds shared department folders, and Shared with me lists files colleagues have shared with you.\nTo work from your PC, install Synology Drive Client (Windows or macOS) from the Get desktop and mobile apps link in the portal, sign in with your NAS account, and create a sync task for the folders you need.\nOn your phone, install the Synology Drive app (iOS or Android) to open, upload and share files while away from the office.\nTo share, right-click a file or folder and choose Share. Invite colleagues by name and pick their permission, or on the Public Link tab create a link and set Password Protection and Link Expiration.\nTo undo a bad change, right-click the file, choose Version history, pick an earlier version and click Restore (or Make a copy to keep both).\nTo recover a deleted file, open Recycle Bin in the left panel and click Restore. Files deleted from a Team Folder go to that folder's recycle bin, which only IT can open.\",\"Version history and the Recycle Bin only work in folders where IT has turned on versioning, so keep work files in Drive rather than only on your PC.\nTo collect files from customers or suppliers who have no NAS account, right-click a folder and choose Request files. They can upload but cannot see anything else.\nFor links to people outside KLAE, always set a password and an expiry date, and untick Allow users to download and copy for sensitive pricing.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal, Desktop app, Mobile app\",\"synology-office, universal-viewer, file-station, hyper-backup, snapshot-replication, synology-photos, universal-search\",\"nodejs-v20, universal-search, synology-application-service, universal-viewer\",\"shared drive, file sharing, sync, onedrive, google drive, dropbox, team folder, previous version, restore file, share link\",,4.0.3-27892,\nsynology-high-availability,Synology High Availability,icons/synology-high-availability.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Business,,IT approval needed,\"Needs a second identical NAS with identical drives, which is a significant cost.\",IT admin,it,Pairs two identical NAS units so the second one takes over automatically if the first one fails.,\"Synology High Availability joins two Synology NAS into an active/passive cluster. The active server runs all services and syncs data to the passive server, which takes over automatically if the active one fails, so staff lose access only briefly. It protects against hardware failure but is not a backup.\",\"Finance: keep the accounting folders available during month-end closing even if a NAS motherboard or power supply fails.\nSales: keep quotation and customer folders reachable for all offices during a hardware failure, instead of waiting days for a repair.\nIT: switch services to the passive server by hand before planned maintenance on the active one.\",\"Buy a second NAS of the same model with the same drives, and update both to the same DSM version (the package needs DSM 7.4).\nConnect the two units directly with a network cable for the heartbeat link and give both static IP addresses.\nOn the active NAS, go to Main Menu > Package Center, install Synology High Availability and open it.\nIn the Cluster section, create the HA cluster and follow the wizard to choose the passive server, the heartbeat interface and the cluster IP address.\nPoint staff drive mappings and servers to the cluster name or IP address, not to the individual units.\nTest a manual switchover after office hours, and check the Service and Log sections afterwards.\",\"All data on the passive server is erased when the cluster is created.\nIt is not a backup: deleted or encrypted files are copied to the passive server too. Keep Hyper Backup running.\nSome packages do not support High Availability; check before planning.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"snapshot-replication, hyper-backup, storage-manager, active-insight\",,\"high availability, failover, cluster, redundancy, uptime, standby nas, sha\",,2.1.6-1745,\nsynology-mailplus,Synology MailPlus,icons/synology-mailplus.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Productivity\",,Approved,Free Synology client for MailPlus Server; installing it also brings in Synology Calendar and Synology Contacts.,End user,all,Webmail and mobile app for email accounts hosted on Synology MailPlus Server.,\"Synology MailPlus is the webmail and mobile client for mailboxes on Synology MailPlus Server. Staff can read and send email in a browser, sort mail with labels and filters, use smart search, and get an AI Summary of long threads if IT enables it in Synology AI Console. It can also add Outlook accounts using OAuth for SMTP and POP3.\",\"Sales: read and answer customer enquiries from any browser, for example at a customer's office or an exhibition booth, without setting up Outlook.\nEngineering: use the MailPlus mobile app on site to receive service requests and send commissioning reports from a phone.\nProcurement: use filters and labels to sort supplier confirmations, delivery notices and invoices automatically.\nManagement: click AI Summary on long email threads with principals, if IT turns on AI for MailPlus in Synology AI Console.\",\"IT installs Synology MailPlus from Package Center. Package Center also installs Synology Calendar and Synology Contacts, which MailPlus depends on.\nOpen it from Main Menu > MailPlus in DSM, or from the app launcher in the Synology Drive web portal.\nRead, write and search email as in any webmail. Set up labels and filters to sort customer and supplier mail into folders automatically.\nBefore leave or a long site visit, turn on an auto-reply in the MailPlus settings.\nOn your phone, install the Synology MailPlus app (iOS or Android) and sign in with the NAS address and your NAS account.\nIf you prefer Outlook, ask IT for the IMAP and SMTP settings of MailPlus Server; Outlook and MailPlus show the same mailbox.\",\"Installing MailPlus also installs Synology Calendar and Synology Contacts, so IT should plan all three together.\nEvery active mailbox uses a MailPlus licence on the server, so ask IT before requesting new email accounts.\nIf AI features are turned on, the email text is sent to an outside AI provider; follow IT's rules on confidential pricing and personal data.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal, Mobile app\",\"synology-mailplus-server, synology-contacts, synology-calendar, synology-ai-console, bitdefender-for-mailplus, universal-viewer\",\"synology-calendar, synology-contacts, synology-mailplus-server, nodejs-v22, synology-application-service, universal-viewer\",\"email, webmail, mail, outlook, inbox, mailbox, auto reply, out of office, mobile email\",,4.1.0-22327,\nsynology-mailplus-server,Synology MailPlus Server,icons/synology-mailplus-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Productivity\",,IT approval needed,\"Five mailboxes are free, extra mailboxes need paid licences, and mail settings affect everyone.\",IT admin,it,\"Hosts company email on the NAS: mailboxes, delivery, spam and virus filtering.\",\"Synology MailPlus Server is the mail server behind Synology MailPlus email accounts. It can send and receive email for a company domain, stores mailboxes on the NAS, filters spam and threats, and checks SPF, DKIM and DMARC to catch spoofed mail; it can also run as a high-availability cluster. Staff reach mail through Outlook (IMAP/POP3 and SMTP), or through the Synology MailPlus webmail and mobile app.\",\"IT: host mailboxes for the company domain on our own hardware, so mail data stays under KLAE's control.\nFinance: SPF, DKIM and DMARC checks help stop spoofed emails pretending to be a supplier asking to change bank details.\nSales: customer enquiries and RFQs arrive in mailboxes protected by spam and virus filtering.\nManagement: role addresses such as sales@ or service@ can be set up as aliases, which need no extra licence and survive staff changes.\",\"Open MailPlus Server from the DSM Main Menu with an administrator account and check Server Management > Mail Monitor for mail traffic and server status.\nOn the Domain page, confirm the company domain, and make sure the MX, SPF, DKIM and DMARC records at our DNS provider match it.\nOn the Account page, activate MailPlus for the users or groups who should have a mailbox; each activated account uses one licence.\nOn the License page, add MailPlus License Pack keys (5 or 20 accounts) when more than five mailboxes are needed.\nReview the Security and Mail Delivery settings (spam, antivirus, sender policies, SMTP authentication), and check Threat Monitor and Queue for blocked or stuck mail.\nGive staff access: either install the Synology MailPlus webmail package (it also brings Calendar and Contacts) or send staff IMAP and SMTP settings for Outlook.\nInclude MailPlus Server in the Hyper Backup schedule and test a restore.\",\"Each NAS includes five free MailPlus licences; aliases of the same account do not need extra licences, and deactivated accounts free their licence for reuse.\nA wrong DNS or delivery setting can stop email for the whole company, so make changes outside office hours and test sending and receiving.\nMailboxes grow quickly; set quotas and watch volume space in Storage Manager.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"synology-mailplus, bitdefender-for-mailplus, synology-contacts, synology-calendar, synology-ai-console, hyper-backup, perl\",perl,\"email server, mail server, exchange, smtp, imap, spam filter, mail licence, mailbox, company email, domain email\",,4.1.0-31778,\nsynology-office,Synology Office,icons/synology-office.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Productivity\",,Approved,\"Free, works with Synology Drive Server and keeps documents on our own NAS.\",End user,\"sales, marketing, engineering, finance, hr, management, procurement\",\"Create and co-edit documents, spreadsheets and slides in the browser, stored on the NAS.\",\"Synology Office is a browser-based office suite for creating documents, spreadsheets and slides inside Synology Drive. Several people can edit the same file at once, leave comments, and every change is saved automatically. Files can be encrypted with a password, Word, Excel and PowerPoint files can be opened as Synology Office copies, and finished work can be downloaded in Microsoft Office or PDF format.\",\"Sales: a salesperson and a product specialist edit the same quotation costing sheet at the same time, without emailing copies back and forth.\nEngineering: keep a shared commissioning checklist or site-survey log that engineers in different regions update live.\nHR: draft the staff handbook or training schedule and collect comments from management in the same file before finalising.\nManagement: collect monthly figures from the regional offices into one shared spreadsheet instead of merging several Excel files.\",\"Open Synology Drive (Main Menu > Synology Drive in DSM, or the Drive portal address).\nGo to the folder you want, click the + (Create) button and choose a document, spreadsheet or slides; it saves as you type. For confidential files such as salary sheets or tender pricing, choose Create > Create an encrypted file and set a password.\nTo work on an existing Word, Excel or PowerPoint file, double-click it in Drive to preview it, then choose View > Open in Synology Office. This creates a Synology Office version of the file.\nTo work together, right-click the file in Drive and choose Share, then give colleagues Edit or Comment only permission. Everyone who opens it sees the others' changes live.\nSelect text or a cell and add a comment to ask a question or suggest a change, instead of editing someone else's work directly.\nTo go back to an earlier version, click the View History icon in the left sidebar of the open file, pick a version and click Restore, or Make a copy to keep both.\nTo send a file outside KLAE, use the File menu to download it in Microsoft Office or PDF format.\",\"Synology Office files (.odoc, .osheet, .oslides) only open in Synology Office, so send customers a downloaded Word, Excel or PDF copy.\nSynology Office files are kept in the Synology Office database, so IT must back up both Synology Drive Server and Synology Office in Hyper Backup.\nSynology Office depends on Synology AI Console; AI writing and formula help only appears if IT turns it on for you.\",\"Web portal, DSM web (Main Menu)\",\"synology-drive-server, synology-ai-console, universal-viewer, document-viewer, synology-chat-server\",\"synology-ai-console, nodejs-v20, synology-application-service, synology-drive-server\",\"word, excel, powerpoint, spreadsheet, google docs, co-editing, online document, slides, collaborate, comment\",,3.7.2-22592,\nsynology-photos,Synology Photos,icons/synology-photos.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Multimedia,,Approved,Keeps company photos on company storage rather than on personal phones or cloud accounts.,End user,\"engineering, marketing, sales, hr\",\"Store, organise and share photos and videos, with automatic backup from phones.\",\"Synology Photos manages photos and videos stored on the NAS. Each user has a Personal Space, and teams can use a Shared Space with folder permissions set by IT. Photos can be grouped into normal or conditional albums, found by date, place or face, shared by link with an expiry date, and backed up automatically from phones with the Synology Photos mobile app.\",\"Engineering: back up site photos of panels, cable routing and nameplates from phones to the NAS, then file them in an album per project for commissioning reports.\nMarketing: one library of product photos, exhibition booths and event pictures, organised in albums for the website and catalogues.\nHR: share training-day and company-event photos with all staff through an album link.\nSales: send a customer an album link showing delivered equipment or a completed installation.\",\"Open Main Menu > Synology Photos in DSM, or go to the Photos address IT gives you (for example https://<nas-address>/photo).\nChoose Personal Space for your own photos, or Shared Space for team photos IT has given you access to.\nUpload from a computer with the Upload option or by dragging files into the browser window.\nOn your phone, install the Synology Photos app (iOS or Android), sign in, then go to More > Enable Photo Backup. Choose Shared Space as the destination only if IT has allowed it.\nCreate an album, add photos, then use Share to create a link. Use the link's password and expiry options for links sent outside KLAE.\nFind photos later by scrolling the timeline by date, or search by place, tag or people.\",\"If iPhone HEIC photos or HEVC videos show no thumbnail, install Synology Image Assistant on your computer; since DSM 7.2.2 these previews are made on your device, not the NAS.\nLet the first phone backup run on office Wi-Fi, as it can be large.\nShared Space permissions in Synology Photos are separate from File Station permissions on the photo folder; ask IT if you can see a folder in one but not the other.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal, Mobile app\",\"synology-drive-server, advanced-media-extensions, file-station, hyper-backup, universal-search\",\"nodejs-v20, synology-application-service\",\"photos, pictures, images, gallery, album, phone backup, site photos, google photos, video\",,1.9.1-10928,\nsynology-tiering-vault,Synology Tiering Vault,icons/synology-tiering-vault.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Utilities\",,IT approval needed,Needs a second Synology NAS on DSM 7.3 or later to act as the cold tier.,IT admin,it,Runs on a second NAS that stores rarely used files moved off the main NAS by Synology Tiering.,\"Synology Tiering moves files that have not been opened or changed for a set time from the main (hot) NAS to a second (cold) Synology NAS, and Synology Tiering Vault is the package that sets up that cold-tier NAS to store them. Staff still open tiered files from the original shared folder on the main NAS, and files that are edited or used often move back automatically. The latest version turns on storage efficiency for cold-tier folders when the volume supports it.\",\"Engineering: move completed project folders and old commissioning photos to a cheaper cold NAS while keeping them in the same folder path.\nMarketing: keep years of product photos and exhibition videos available without filling the main NAS.\nIT: free space on the main NAS without buying bigger drives or making staff look for files somewhere else.\",\"Prepare a second Synology NAS on DSM 7.3 or later with a Btrfs volume and at least 2 GB of RAM.\nOn that cold-tier NAS, go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for Synology Tiering Vault and click Install.\nOn our main (hot-tier) NAS, install Synology Tiering and connect it to the cold-tier NAS.\nCreate a tiering plan: choose the Btrfs shared folders and the rules, for example files not opened for 365 days, or when free space falls below a set level.\nSet how often tiering runs and check the logs after the first run.\nManage files only through the main NAS; never edit or delete tiered files directly on the cold tier.\",\"Hybrid Share, encrypted and compressed shared folders cannot be tiered.\nA 1 Gbps network link is the minimum and 10 Gbps is recommended.\nBack up both tiers at the same point in time; restoring only one tier with Hyper Backup can cause missing or mismatched files.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"storage-manager, storage-analyzer, hyper-backup, universal-search\",,\"tiering, cold storage, archive, old files, free space, hot tier, cold tier\",,1.3.0-0508,\ntext-editor,Text Editor,icons/text-editor.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Approved,A small Synology tool for technical staff.,End user,\"it, swe, engineering\",\"Edit plain-text, CSV, script and config files on the NAS directly in the browser.\",\"Text Editor is a simple editor in DSM for plain-text files such as scripts, HTML, CSV and configuration files stored on the NAS. Small changes can be made without downloading and re-uploading the file. It has tabs, find and replace, line numbers, code highlighting and a choice of character encoding, for files up to 10 MB.\",\"IT: fix a configuration file or script stored on the NAS without copying it to a PC first.\nSWE: make a quick correction to a README, HTML page, JSON file or script in a shared folder.\nEngineering: check or correct a CSV tag list or device configuration export before loading it into an HMI or PLC project.\",\"In File Station, right-click a text file and choose Open with Text Editor, or drag one or more files from File Station into the Text Editor window.\nOr open Main Menu > Text Editor and use File > Open to choose a file, picking a character encoding if the text looks wrong.\nUse Search > Find or Search > Replace to find text or change it throughout the file.\nSave with File > Save, which overwrites the file, or File > Save As to keep the original and choose a new name, folder and encoding.\nClose a tab with File > Close; Text Editor warns you if there are unsaved changes.\",\"Files larger than 10 MB cannot be opened.\nUse File > Save As to keep a copy before editing configuration files, so you can go back.\nIt only handles plain text; use Synology Office or Microsoft Office for .docx or .xlsx files.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"file-station, synology-drive-server, universal-viewer, web-station\",,\"text editor, notepad, edit txt, csv, config file, code editor, script, log file\",,1.2.6-0260,\nuniversal-search,Universal Search,icons/universal-search.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Approved,\"Synology Drive Server depends on it, so do not uninstall it while Drive Server is installed.\",End user,all,\"One search box for files, photos and notes on the NAS, by file name or by text inside documents.\",\"Universal Search lets you search the NAS from one place, covering files in shared folders, photos and notes. IT chooses which folders are indexed, and indexed folders can be searched by file name or by the text inside the documents. Synology Drive Server, Active Backup for Google Workspace and Active Backup for Microsoft 365 depend on it.\",\"Sales: type a customer or project name to find old quotations and tender documents spread across several shared folders.\nEngineering: search for a model or part number, such as an MTL barrier or BEKA indicator, to find datasheets and loop drawings that mention it.\nFinance: find a supplier invoice or payment record by its number when the folder is indexed by content.\nMarketing: find product photos and brochure files by name across shared folders and photo libraries in one search.\",\"Sign in to DSM and open Main Menu > Universal Search.\nType a word in the search box, such as a file name, customer name or part number, and press Enter.\nNarrow the results to one type, such as files, photos or notes, if the list is long.\nOpen a result to preview it, or go to the folder where it is stored.\nIf text inside documents in a folder cannot be found, ask IT to add that folder to the index. IT does this in Preferences > File Indexing > Indexed Folder List.\nIf results look out of date, IT can run Preferences > File Indexing > Check Index Database.\",\"You only see results from folders you already have permission to open.\nScanned PDFs that are only images usually cannot be found by their content, so give them clear file names.\nContent indexing uses CPU and disk space. IT should index work folders only, not backup or video archives.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"file-station, synology-drive-server, synology-photos, note-station, synology-tiering-vault, active-backup-for-google-workspace, active-backup-for-microsoft-365\",,\"search, find file, find document, search inside pdf, full text search, index, where is my file, lookup\",,1.9.0-0900,\nuniversal-viewer,Universal Viewer,icons/universal-viewer.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Approved,Synology system component; keep it updated.,IT admin,it,Background component that lets Synology Drive and MailPlus preview many file types without downloading.,\"Universal Viewer lets staff view many file formats directly in Synology Drive, so they can double-click a PDF, image, text or Office file instead of downloading it; Synology Drive Server and MailPlus require it. Since version 1.4.0 it previews images up to 200 MB, PDFs up to 500 MB and PSD files up to 1 GB, and supports WebP/JFIF images, PDF comments and clickable links, files inside compressed archives, and encrypted OpenOffice files.\",\"Sales: preview a principal's price list or datasheet in Drive without downloading it to a shared office PC.\nEngineering: check a drawing PDF or site photo in Drive from any browser before deciding to download it.\nIT: fewer copies of company files left in the Downloads folders of shared or personal computers.\",\"Check in Package Center > Installed that Universal Viewer shows as running, and install updates when Package Center shows them.\nUpdate it together with Synology Drive Server, since Drive relies on it for previews.\nDo not uninstall it; Synology Drive Server and MailPlus depend on it, and Drive web previews stop working without it.\nTo test, open Synology Drive and double-click a PDF or image, or right-click a file and choose Preview.\nIf a large file will not preview, check the limits: images up to 200 MB, PDFs up to 500 MB and PSD files up to 1 GB.\",\"Staff never open it directly; they only see it as the preview window in Synology Drive.\nPreview is view-only; to edit an Office file use View > Open in Synology Office or download it.\",Background service,\"synology-drive-server, synology-office, document-viewer, pdf-viewer, universal-search, synology-mailplus\",,\"preview, file preview, view file, drive preview, open file in browser, thumbnail\",,1.4.0-0712,\nusb-copy,USB Copy,icons/usb-copy.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Backup, Utilities, Productivity\",,Approved,\"IT controls which USB drives are used, to avoid malware and data leaks.\",IT admin,it,\"Copies files between the NAS and USB drives or SD cards, and can start as soon as a device is plugged in.\",\"USB Copy runs copy tasks between NAS shared folders and USB drives or SD cards connected to the NAS. Tasks can import files to the NAS or export them to the device, using incremental, mirror or multi-versioned modes with file filters, and can start automatically when a device is plugged in without opening DSM. It is useful for offline backup drives and for bringing in photos from camera cards.\",\"IT: export a weekly copy of key shared folders to rotating USB drives kept offsite, as an offline backup that ransomware cannot reach.\nMarketing: import product and exhibition photos from camera SD cards straight into the marketing photo folder.\nFinance: keep a monthly offline copy of closed accounting folders on a company-owned encrypted USB drive stored in the safe.\",\"Go to Main Menu > Package Center, search for USB Copy and click Install.\nConnect a USB drive or SD card to the NAS and open USB Copy.\nCreate a task and choose the direction: import to the NAS or export to the USB device.\nIn Task Settings, pick the source and destination folders and the copy mode: multi-versioned, mirror or incremental.\nIn Trigger Time, choose when it runs: when the device is plugged in, on a schedule, or manually; add rules in File Filter if needed.\nCheck the Overview after it runs, then eject the device before unplugging it.\",\"Mirror mode deletes files at the destination that no longer exist at the source; use multi-versioned mode for backups.\nOnly use company-owned drives, and scan drives from outside before importing.\nUnplug backup drives after the copy so ransomware cannot reach them.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Background service\",\"hyper-backup, storage-manager, file-station, synology-photos\",,\"usb, external drive, sd card, copy files, offline backup, camera, import photos, export\",,2.2.1-1306,\nvirtual-machine-manager,Virtual Machine Manager,icons/virtual-machine-manager.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Business, Utilities\",,IT approval needed,\"It uses a lot of NAS memory and CPU, can need a paid licence, and Windows guests need their own licences.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",\"Runs virtual Windows, Linux or DSM machines on the NAS, so IT doesn't need to buy a separate server.\",\"Virtual Machine Manager is Synology's tool for creating and running virtual machines on the NAS. IT can run Windows, Linux or Virtual DSM as separate computers that share the NAS hardware, with snapshots to roll a machine back after a bad change. It depends on Replication Service and SAN Manager. A paid Pro licence adds advanced features, and every supported NAS can use a one-time 30-day trial of them.\",\"Engineering: keep a Windows virtual machine with older HMI and PLC configuration software, so engineers can still open legacy customer project files without keeping an old laptop.\nSWE: create disposable test machines to try software builds or Windows updates before they reach staff PCs.\nIT: run a small Windows or Linux server, such as a software licence server, on the NAS instead of buying separate hardware.\nIT: test a DSM update in a Virtual DSM machine before applying it to the production NAS.\",\"Check on synology.com that our NAS model supports Virtual Machine Manager, and confirm there is spare RAM for the machines you plan to run.\nInstall Virtual Machine Manager from Package Center (this also installs Replication Service and SAN Manager), then open Main Menu > Virtual Machine Manager and complete the first-time setup.\nCheck the host, storage and network settings under Overview, Storage and Network, then upload the operating system installer under Image.\nGo to Virtual Machine > Create, choose the operating system, then set the CPU cores, memory, virtual disk and network.\nPower on the machine, click Connect to open its console in the browser and finish installing the operating system.\nInstall Synology Guest Tool inside the virtual machine, then set up snapshots under Protection and add the machine to the NAS backup plan.\nIf a Pro licence is approved, activate it under License. The NAS must be online during activation.\",\"Every running virtual machine takes RAM and CPU away from file sharing; size machines carefully so the NAS stays responsive for all offices.\nWindows virtual machines need their own valid Windows licences. Some advanced features need a Virtual Machine Manager Pro licence.\nGive staff access through Remote Desktop on the office network or VPN, not through ports opened on the router.\",DSM web (Main Menu),\"container-manager, snapshot-replication, hyper-backup, storage-manager, vpn-server, replication-service, san-manager\",\"replication-service, san-manager\",\"virtual machine, vm, virtualization, windows server, test machine, hypervisor, virtual dsm, remote desktop\",,2.8.0-13004,\nvpn-server,VPN Server,icons/vpn-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Utilities, Management\",,IT approval needed,\"It changes network security for the whole office, so IT must plan protocols, ports and users first.\",IT admin,\"it, engineering, sales\",Turns the NAS into a VPN server so staff outside the office can reach internal resources securely.,\"VPN Server turns the NAS into a VPN server that supports OpenVPN, L2TP/IPSec and PPTP. Staff at regional offices or customer sites connect with a VPN client and reach office resources over an encrypted connection. IT controls which users may connect and can see active connections and logs.\",\"Engineering: service engineers at customer plants connect to HQ and open project files and drawings on their usual mapped network drives.\nSales: staff working from customer sites or hotels reach shared quotation folders over an encrypted connection on public Wi-Fi.\nSWE: developers reach internal test servers and Git repositories from outside without exposing them to the internet.\nIT: give the Butterworth, Kemaman, Pasir Gudang and Bintulu/Kuching offices access to services that should not be opened through QuickConnect.\",\"After approval, install VPN Server from Package Center and open Main Menu > VPN Server.\nUnder Set up VPN Server, choose OpenVPN or L2TP/IPSec, enable it, and set the client IP range, the maximum number of connections and whether clients may access the server's LAN.\nOn the office router, forward the matching ports to the NAS: UDP 1194 for OpenVPN, or UDP 500, 1701 and 4500 for L2TP/IPSec.\nIn Privilege, allow only the staff accounts that need VPN, and only for the protocol you use.\nFor OpenVPN, click Export configuration and give users the file with instructions to import it into the OpenVPN client on their laptop or phone.\nCheck Connection List and Log regularly for unknown users or repeated failed connections.\",\"Do not use PPTP; its encryption is weak. Use OpenVPN or L2TP/IPSec.\nVPN does not work through QuickConnect. The NAS needs a public IP or a DDNS hostname (Control Panel > External Access > DDNS) plus port forwarding.\nFor L2TP/IPSec, use a long random pre-shared key and share it only through a secure channel.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Desktop app, Mobile app\",\"quickconnect, secure-signin-service, smb-service, radius-server, log-center, presto-file-server\",,\"vpn, remote access, connect to office, work from site, openvpn, l2tp, secure connection, tunnel\",,1.4.10-2984,\nweb-station,Web Station,icons/web-station.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,IT approval needed,\"It is published by Synology, but every site it hosts opens web access to the NAS and runs on open-source runtimes, so IT must review each one.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",Synology's web hosting manager for running internal websites and web apps on the NAS.,\"Web Station is Synology's control panel for hosting websites on the NAS. IT uses it to set up web services and portals (hostname, port or alias), choose the web server (Nginx by default, or Apache HTTP Server 2.4) and the PHP version for each site. It can also run Node.js and Python sites as containers through Container Manager, and it is the base that phpMyAdmin, WordPress and similar packages run on.\",\"SWE: host internal tools built in-house, such as a stock lookup page or a quotation calculator, on the office network.\nIT: run phpMyAdmin and other admin web pages from one place, with access limited to the office network.\nMarketing: preview a new product landing page internally before it goes to the external website host.\nProcurement: use internal web tools from SWE, such as a warehouse stock report, without the company paying for separate hosting.\",\"Open Main Menu > Web Station. The sections are Overview, Web Portal, Web Service, Script Language Settings and Error Page Settings.\nOn Overview, check the status of the default server, personal websites and the web service portal. Also check the back-end packages (such as Nginx, Apache HTTP Server, PHP and Python) and the service packages (such as WordPress, MediaWiki and phpMyAdmin).\nFor PHP sites, go to Script Language Settings and create or edit a PHP profile (PHP version, extensions and core settings).\nGo to Web Service, click Create and choose the type: static website, native script language website, or containerized script language website (the containerized type needs Container Manager).\nChoose the document root (normally a folder in the shared folder named web), the HTTP back-end server and the PHP profile.\nGo to Web Portal and create a portal for the service, using a hostname, port or alias so users can reach it. Set custom error pages in Error Page Settings if needed.\nTest the site from a browser on the office network, then limit who can reach it in Control Panel > Security > Firewall.\",\"Do not forward web ports on the office router for internal sites. Remote staff should connect through VPN Server.\nUse PHP 8.4 for in-house sites. Keep PHP 8.2 while phpMyAdmin or Note Station is installed, because they need it, but its security support ends on 31 December 2026.\nVersion 4.3.1 adds compatibility checks that prevent conflicts between Synology Tiering and shared folders that Web Station uses.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Web portal\",\"apache-http-server-2-4, php-8-4, php-8-3, mariadb-10, phpmyadmin, container-manager, nodejs-v22, php-8-2\",,\"website, web server, web hosting, intranet, internal site, nginx, web page, host a site\",,4.3.1-0530,\nwebdav-server,WebDAV Server,icons/webdav-server.png,Synology,Synology Inc.,Synology Inc.,\"Utilities, Management\",,IT approval needed,\"Install or keep it only if an app really needs WebDAV, and allow HTTPS only.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",Lets WebDAV-capable apps and file browsers open NAS folders like a network drive over HTTP or HTTPS.,\"WebDAV Server lets WebDAV clients, such as some Windows apps, macOS Finder and Linux file browsers, open NAS shared folders like a network drive over HTTP or HTTPS. It also has a Calendar section for CalDAV clients. Most KLAE staff do not need it, because Synology Drive and mapped network drives cover everyday file access.\",\"SWE: connect a development or document tool that only supports WebDAV to a project folder on the NAS.\nEngineering: let a tablet file manager app that supports WebDAV open drawings on the NAS where the Synology Drive app cannot be used.\nIT: if WebDAV Server is installed but no app uses it, turn it off so fewer services are exposed.\",\"Open Main Menu > WebDAV Server.\nOn the settings page, untick Enable HTTP (port 5005) and keep only Enable HTTPS (port 5006). If nothing uses WebDAV, turn both off.\nUnder Advanced, keep Enable Anonymous WebDAV off, leave DavDepthInfinity off unless an app requires it, and turn on the WebDAV log so you can see who connects.\nSet speed limits if WebDAV transfers slow down other users.\nGive users the address https://<nas-address>:5006. They sign in with their NAS account and see only the shared folders they already have permission to open.\nUse the Calendar section only if a CalDAV calendar client needs it.\",\"Do not forward port 5005 (HTTP) on the router; passwords would travel unencrypted.\nFor everyday file access, Synology Drive and SMB network drives are easier for staff and better supported.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Network drive\",\"smb-service, synology-drive-server, file-station, synology-calendar, vpn-server\",,\"webdav, caldav, network drive, remote folder, dav, http file access, calendar sync, finder connect\",,2.4.8-20135,\napache-http-server-2-4,Apache HTTP Server 2.4,icons/apache-http-server-2-4.png,Open Source,apache.org,Synology Inc.,Development Tools,,IT approval needed,\"Synology publishes it, but it is open-source web server software for IT and SWE, so IT must review which sites use it.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",Optional Apache web server that Web Station can use instead of Nginx to run a website.,\"Apache HTTP Server 2.4 is the open-source web server from apache.org, packaged and published by Synology in Package Center. It lets IT choose Apache instead of the default Nginx as the back-end server for a Web Station site, which some web applications need for .htaccess files and rewrite rules. It needs Web Station and has no window of its own.\",\"SWE: run an internal PHP tool that uses .htaccess rewrite rules, such as a parts lookup page, without converting its rules for Nginx.\nIT: switch one site to Apache for compatibility while the other sites stay on Nginx.\nSales: rely on internal web tools from SWE, such as a quotation calculator, that need Apache to run.\",\"Open Main Menu > Web Station (Apache has no window of its own).\nGo to Web Service, select the site that needs Apache and click Edit.\nSet the HTTP back-end server to Apache HTTP Server 2.4 and save.\nPut any .htaccess file the application needs in the site's document root.\nOpen the site in a browser on the office network to test it, and check Log Center or the application's logs if pages fail.\",\"Nginx is the Web Station default. Only switch the sites that need Apache features.\nBefore uninstalling it, check Web Station for sites that use it and Package Center for packages that depend on it (the WordPress, Joomla, MediaWiki and vtiger CRM packages need it).\nRecent package versions fix security issues, including CVE-2024-38474, CVE-2024-38475 and CVE-2024-38477. Install updates soon after release.\",Background service,\"web-station, php-8-4, php-8-3, phpmyadmin, mariadb-10, wordpress, joomla, mediawiki, vtigercrm\",web-station,\"apache, httpd, web server, htaccess, rewrite rules, website engine, web hosting\",,2.4.63-0155,\ncontainer-manager,Container Manager,icons/container-manager.png,Open Source,Docker Inc.,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,IT approval needed,\"Synology publishes it, but container images from Docker Hub are third-party software that IT must vet before use.\",Developer,\"it, swe\",Synology's Docker-based tool for running apps in separate containers on the NAS.,\"Container Manager is Synology's package for Docker, the lightweight virtualization engine from Docker Inc., published by Synology in Package Center. IT and developers can download images from Docker Hub, which is built in as an image registry, run them as containers, and manage apps made of several containers as projects using Docker Compose files. Synology packages such as Document Viewer and ActiveProtect Vault depend on it.\",\"SWE: run a test database or a newer Node.js or Python version in a container without changing the packages installed on the NAS.\nEngineering: with SWE help, run a test MQTT broker or similar service to check gateway and HMI settings before a site commissioning.\nIT: host a vetted internal tool as a Compose project that is easy to back up, move and rebuild.\nIT: keep ActiveProtect Vault and Document Viewer working, because both depend on Container Manager.\",\"Open Main Menu > Container Manager.\nUnder Registry, search for the image you need. Prefer Docker Official Images or verified publishers, and get IT approval before downloading.\nUnder Image, check the downloaded image and its tag. Use a fixed version tag rather than latest for anything long-term.\nFor apps with several containers, go to Project > Create, choose a folder for the project and create or upload its docker-compose.yml file.\nMap only the shared folders and ports the container needs, set memory limits, then start it.\nUse the Container and Log pages to check status, resource use and errors.\",\"Docker Hub images are third-party software. IT must check who publishes each image, which version is used and how it will be updated.\nDo not stop or uninstall Container Manager while ActiveProtect Vault or Document Viewer is installed, because both depend on it.\nContainers share the NAS's CPU and RAM with file sharing. Set resource limits and remove containers and images that are no longer used.\",\"DSM web (Main Menu), Command line\",\"activeprotect-vault, web-station, virtual-machine-manager, git-server, mariadb-10, nodejs-v22, document-viewer, pacs\",,\"docker, container, compose, docker hub, image, run apps, self-hosted, containers\",,24.0.2-1706,\ngit-server,Git Server,icons/git-server.png,Open Source,Git,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,IT approval needed,\"Synology publishes it, but it is open-source developer tooling that needs SSH access to the NAS, so IT controls who uses it.\",Developer,\"swe, it\",Hosts Git code repositories on the NAS so developers can push and pull code over SSH.,\"Git Server adds Git, the open-source version control system, to the NAS so it can host source-code repositories. Synology publishes the package; the software comes from the Git project. Developers clone, push and pull over SSH, and IT ticks Allow access for each DSM account that may use it; there is no web interface, issue tracker or pull requests.\",\"SWE: keep the master copy of internal tools and customer project code on the NAS instead of on individual laptops.\nEngineering: rely on SWE keeping versioned commissioning scripts and configuration templates, so any earlier version can be recovered.\nIT: protect all repositories with the normal NAS snapshots and backups.\nManagement: keep source code on company hardware, not in developers' personal accounts.\",\"Make sure SSH is turned on in Control Panel > Terminal & SNMP. Use a non-default port and keep it closed to the internet.\nOpen Main Menu > Git Server. It lists the DSM user accounts, each with an Allow access checkbox. Tick it only for developers who need it, and keep guest and other non-developer accounts unticked.\nCreate a shared folder for repositories (for example, git) in Control Panel > Shared Folder and give developers read/write permission.\nSign in over SSH and create a bare repository, for example: git init --bare /volume1/git/project.git (the volume name may differ).\nOn the developer's PC, clone it with: git clone ssh://username@nas-address:port/volume1/git/project.git\nProtect the repository folder with Snapshot Replication and Hyper Backup.\",\"Use SSH keys instead of passwords, and remove access as soon as a developer leaves.\nThere is no web interface, code review or issue tracking. If SWE needs these, ask IT to review a vetted tool running in Container Manager.\",\"Command line, DSM web (Main Menu)\",\"container-manager, snapshot-replication, hyper-backup, web-station\",,\"git, source code, repository, version control, code backup, repo, ssh\",,2.39.1-1079,\njoomla,Joomla,icons/joomla.png,Open Source,Joomla Leadership Team,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Not recommended,\"There is no clear KLAE need, it depends on PHP 8.2 (security support ends 31 December 2026), and public websites should not run on the NAS that holds company files.\",IT admin,it,Open-source website builder (CMS). KLAE has no need for it.,\"Joomla is an open-source content management system (CMS) for building websites with pages, menus and user logins. Synology publishes the package in Package Center; the software comes from the Joomla project. It needs Web Station, Apache HTTP Server 2.4, PHP 8.2 and MariaDB 10, and KLAE has no planned use for it.\",\"Marketing: keep the company website with an external managed web host, not on the office NAS.\nHR & Admin: put internal notices and procedures in Synology Drive, Synology Office or Synology Chat, which IT already supports.\nIT: avoid running another web application that needs regular PHP, database and plugin security updates.\",\"Do not install it without written approval from IT and Management.\nIf approved, note that Package Center also installs what it needs: Web Station, Apache HTTP Server 2.4, PHP 8.2 and MariaDB 10.\nInstall Joomla from Package Center and follow the wizard, which asks for MariaDB 10 details to create its database.\nOpen the site in a browser, sign in as the administrator and set user permissions.\nKeep Joomla and its extensions updated, and limit access to the office network or VPN.\",\"Every CMS login page is a target for attackers. Never make it reachable from the internet without IT review.\nIt needs PHP 8.2, whose security support ends on 31 December 2026.\",Web portal,\"wordpress, mediawiki, web-station, mariadb-10, php-8-2, apache-http-server-2-4\",\"apache-http-server-2-4, mariadb-10, php-8-2, web-station\",\"joomla, cms, website builder, content management, web pages, site builder\",,4.4.13-1205,\nmariadb-10,MariaDB 10,icons/mariadb-10.png,Open Source,MariaDB Foundation,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,IT approval needed,\"Synology publishes it, but it is open-source database software for IT and SWE. IT controls the accounts, network access and backups.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",Open-source MySQL-compatible database server used by web apps and phpMyAdmin on the NAS.,\"MariaDB 10 is an open-source, MySQL-compatible database server from the MariaDB Foundation, published by Synology in Package Center. It stores data for web applications run through Web Station and is managed with phpMyAdmin or other SQL tools. Its window has four sections: User Account, Connection, InnoDB Buffer Pool and Information.\",\"SWE: store data for internal tools, such as a service-report log or stock lookup, in one central database.\nIT: provide the database that phpMyAdmin and Web Station applications need.\nProcurement: use SWE-built warehouse tools that keep their data in MariaDB and are backed up with the NAS.\",\"Open Main Menu > MariaDB 10. The window has User Account, Connection, InnoDB Buffer Pool and Information sections.\nUnder User Account, use Change Password to set a strong root password and store it in the IT password manager. Reset root password is there if the password is lost.\nUnder Connection, tick Enable TCP/IP connection (port 3306) only if applications on other computers must connect.\nUnder InnoDB Buffer Pool, raise the buffer pool size only if databases are slow, and do not allocate more memory than the NAS can spare.\nUnder Information, note the domain socket (/run/mysqld/mysqld10.sock) that applications on the NAS itself can use.\nIn phpMyAdmin, create a separate database and user for each application instead of using root.\nBack up the databases with Hyper Backup or scheduled exports, and test a restore from time to time.\",\"Never open port 3306 to the internet. Keep TCP/IP access limited to the office network, or turn it off.\nRestoring data backed up from a newer MariaDB 10 package version is not supported. Restore onto a package that is at least as new as the backup.\nThe auth_gssapi plugin is now a separate dynamic module. If an app uses GSSAPI (Kerberos) logins, IT must configure it manually in my.cnf.\",\"Background service, DSM web (Main Menu)\",\"phpmyadmin, web-station, php-8-4, hyper-backup, wordpress\",,\"database, mysql, mariadb, sql, db server, tables, data storage\",,10.11.11-1551,\nmediawiki,MediaWiki,icons/mediawiki.png,Open Source,MediaWiki,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Not recommended,\"There is no clear KLAE need, because Note Station, Synology Office and Synology Drive already cover shared knowledge. It also depends on PHP 8.2 (security support ends 31 December 2026).\",IT admin,it,Open-source wiki software (the engine behind Wikipedia). KLAE has no need for it.,\"MediaWiki is the open-source wiki software used by Wikipedia, published by Synology in Package Center. Many people can write and link pages, and every change is kept in the page history. It needs Web Station, Apache HTTP Server 2.4, PHP 8.2 and MariaDB 10.\",\"Engineering: keep product notes, wiring tips and commissioning checklists in Synology Office or Note Station, which staff already know.\nHR & Admin: keep staff handbooks and procedures in Synology Drive with folder permissions, without a separate wiki login.\nIT: avoid maintaining another web application that needs PHP and database updates.\",\"Before asking for it, check whether Synology Office, Note Station or Synology Drive can meet the need.\nIf IT and Management approve it, note that Package Center also installs what it needs: Web Station, Apache HTTP Server 2.4, PHP 8.2 and MariaDB 10.\nInstall MediaWiki from Package Center and follow the wizard to connect it to MariaDB 10.\nOpen the wiki in a browser, sign in as the administrator and set who can read and edit pages.\nKeep it updated and allow access only from the office network or VPN.\",\"A wiki needs someone to own its content. Without an owner, pages quickly go out of date.\nWiki accounts are separate from DSM accounts unless IT sets up extra integration.\",Web portal,\"note-station, synology-office, synology-drive-server, joomla, wordpress, php-8-2, apache-http-server-2-4\",\"apache-http-server-2-4, mariadb-10, php-8-2, web-station\",\"wiki, knowledge base, mediawiki, documentation, how-to pages, intranet\",,1.43.5-1211,\nnodejs-v18,Node.js v18,icons/nodejs-v18.png,Open Source,nodejs.org,Synology Inc.,Development Tools,,IT approval needed,\"Keep it only while Synology packages such as Synology Chat Server need it. It reached end-of-life on 30 April 2025, so do not build in-house apps on it.\",Developer,\"swe, it\",Node.js 18 runtime that Synology packages such as Chat Server need. Support ended on 30 April 2025.,\"Node.js runs JavaScript outside a web browser. This package comes from the Node.js project (nodejs.org) and is published by Synology in Package Center; Synology packages can depend on it, and installing Synology Chat Server, for example, also installs it. The Node.js project ended support for version 18 on 30 April 2025, so no in-house apps should run on it.\",\"IT: keep it while a Synology package such as Synology Chat Server depends on it. Package Center shows which packages depend on it.\nSWE: move any in-house scripts or apps that still use Node.js 18 to Node.js v22.\nManagement: removing the runtime when no package needs it lowers the security risk on the NAS that holds company files.\",\"Open Package Center > Installed > Node.js v18 and install updates when Package Center shows them.\nCheck the package page in Package Center to see which installed packages depend on it.\nCheck Control Panel > Task Scheduler and the SWE script folders for in-house scripts that use Node.js 18, and move them to Node.js v22.\nIf no installed package or in-house script needs it, IT may stop it and uninstall it after a test period.\nIf Synology Chat Server is installed, Package Center also installs Node.js v18, because Chat Server depends on it.\",\"End-of-life since 30 April 2025. Use Node.js v22 (maintained until 30 April 2027) for in-house work.\nInstall Node.js and PHP updates in a planned maintenance window soon after Package Center shows them.\nNever uninstall it while a Synology package that depends on it is installed, or that package will stop working.\",\"Command line, Background service\",\"synology-chat-server, nodejs-v22, nodejs-v20, synology-application-service\",,\"node, nodejs, node 18, javascript, runtime, npm, chat server, end of life\",,18.20.8-1016,\nnodejs-v20,Node.js v20,icons/nodejs-v20.png,Open Source,nodejs.org,Synology Inc.,Development Tools,,IT approval needed,\"Synology Drive Server, Synology Office and Synology Photos need it, so keep it installed and updated while any of them is installed. Do not build new in-house apps on it: the Node.js project ended support on 30 April 2026.\",Developer,\"it, swe\",\"Node.js 20 runtime needed by Synology Drive Server, Office and Photos. Keep it updated; build nothing on it.\",\"Node.js runs JavaScript outside a web browser. This package comes from the Node.js project (nodejs.org) and is published by Synology in Package Center; it is a required component of Synology Drive Server, Synology Office and Synology Photos. The Node.js project ended support for version 20 on 30 April 2026, but Synology decides when its own packages move to a newer Node.js version.\",\"IT: keep Node.js v20 running and updated, because Synology Drive Server, Synology Office and Synology Photos stop working without it.\nSales: keep quotations and price lists in Synology Drive and Synology Office, which both need this runtime in the background.\nSWE: build in-house apps on Node.js v22, not v20, and move any existing v20 scripts to v22.\nIT: watch Package Center updates for Drive, Office and Photos. Synology decides when they move to a newer Node.js version.\",\"Open Package Center > Installed > Node.js v20 and install updates when Package Center shows them, in a planned maintenance window.\nCheck the package page in Package Center to see which installed packages depend on it.\nDo not stop or uninstall it while Synology Drive Server, Synology Office or Synology Photos is installed.\nKeep Synology Drive Server, Synology Office and Synology Photos updated too. Synology moves them to a newer Node.js version through those updates.\nMove any in-house scripts or apps that still use Node.js 20 to Node.js v22, and test each one.\nReview Node.js v20 again only when Package Center shows that no installed package depends on it.\",\"The Node.js project ended support for version 20 on 30 April 2026. Keep it only for the Synology packages that need it, and use Node.js v22 (maintained until 30 April 2027) for in-house work.\nInstall Node.js and PHP updates in a planned maintenance window soon after Package Center shows them.\nRemoving Node.js v20 would break Synology Drive Server, Synology Office and Synology Photos.\",\"Command line, Background service\",\"synology-drive-server, synology-office, synology-photos, nodejs-v22, nodejs-v18, synology-application-service\",,\"node, nodejs, node 20, javascript, runtime, npm, synology drive, dependency\",,20.20.2-1018,\nnodejs-v22,Node.js v22,icons/nodejs-v22.png,Open Source,nodejs.org,Synology Inc.,Development Tools,,IT approval needed,\"Synology publishes it, but it is an open-source runtime for SWE and IT. Use it for all in-house apps. Synology Contacts and Synology MailPlus need it.\",Developer,\"swe, it\",Node.js 22 JavaScript runtime. This is the supported Node.js version for in-house work until April 2027.,\"Node.js runs JavaScript outside a web browser, for example web back-ends, scheduled scripts and developer tools. This package comes from nodejs.org and is published by Synology in Package Center; Synology Contacts and Synology MailPlus depend on it, so installing either one also installs it. Node.js 22 gets maintenance (security and critical fixes) until 30 April 2027, so all in-house Node.js work should use this version.\",\"SWE: run a scheduled script that converts principals' price lists into the format used by Sales quotation templates.\nSWE: build and test Node.js web apps that run through Web Station or Container Manager, and move apps off Node.js 18 and 20 to this version.\nIT: keep it installed and updated while Synology Contacts or Synology MailPlus is installed, because both need it.\nProcurement: receive stock reports that SWE scripts generate on the NAS on a schedule.\",\"Open Package Center > Installed > Node.js v22 and install updates when Package Center shows them.\nCheck the package page in Package Center to see which installed packages depend on it, and do not uninstall it while any are installed.\nSign in over SSH and run node -v. If several Node.js versions are installed, make sure scripts call the Node.js 22 program.\nKeep each app in its own folder in a shared folder, with its package.json and lock file.\nRun scheduled scripts from Control Panel > Task Scheduler > Create > Scheduled Task > User-defined script.\nFor web apps, use Web Station's containerized script language website option (this needs Container Manager), or a vetted container.\",\"Maintenance support ends on 30 April 2027. Plan the move to the next LTS version (Node.js 24) during early 2027.\nInstall Node.js and PHP updates in a planned maintenance window soon after Package Center shows them.\nThird-party npm libraries are the main security risk. Use well-known packages and run npm audit before deploying.\",\"Command line, Background service\",\"nodejs-v20, nodejs-v18, web-station, container-manager, git-server, synology-contacts, synology-mailplus\",,\"node, nodejs, node 22, javascript, runtime, npm, script, js\",,22.22.3-1010,\npacs,PACS,icons/pacs.png,Open Source,dcm4che.org,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Not recommended,This medical imaging system has no KLAE business need.,IT admin,it,Medical imaging archive for clinics and hospitals. KLAE has no need for it.,\"PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication System) stores and shares medical images such as X-ray, CT and MRI scans in the DICOM format, for clinics and hospitals. Synology publishes the package, which is built from the open-source dcm4che archive (dcm4che.org) with the Weasis viewer, Keycloak and WildFly, and runs on Container Manager. KLAE does not handle medical images.\",\"Engineering: keep site photos, wiring diagrams and panel drawings in Synology Drive, not in a medical archive.\nMarketing: manage product and exhibition photos in Synology Photos.\nIT: avoid running a specialised system that nobody at KLAE can support.\",\"Do not install it. KLAE has no medical imaging data.\nStore photos in Synology Photos and documents or drawings in Synology Drive.\nIf a customer project ever needs a DICOM test system, SWE should raise it with IT for a separate, isolated test setup. Package Center lists Container Manager and DSM 7.4 or later as its requirements.\nIf it is ever found installed, IT should stop it and uninstall it from Package Center > Installed.\",\"Medical images are sensitive personal data with strict privacy rules. KLAE should not store them.\nIt runs several server components in containers, which adds load on the NAS and extra maintenance for IT.\",Web portal,\"synology-photos, synology-drive-server, file-station, container-manager\",container-manager,\"pacs, dicom, medical imaging, x-ray, radiology, scan archive\",,5.30.0-1455,\nperl,Perl,icons/perl.png,Open Source,Perl.org,Synology Inc.,Development Tools,,IT approval needed,\"Synology publishes it as an open-source runtime for IT and SWE use only. Synology MailPlus Server needs it, so keep it installed and updated while MailPlus Server is installed.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",\"Perl scripting runtime. Synology MailPlus Server needs it, so keep it while MailPlus Server is installed.\",\"Perl is an open-source scripting language from Perl.org, published by Synology in Package Center. Synology MailPlus Server depends on it. It has no window of its own; scripts and other packages use it in the background.\",\"IT: keep it installed and updated, because Synology MailPlus Server stops working without it.\nIT: run existing admin scripts, such as log clean-up or usage reports, through Task Scheduler.\nSWE: keep older Perl scripts working until they are rewritten in a language the team maintains.\",\"Open Package Center > Installed > Perl, check its status and install updates when Package Center shows them.\nCheck the package page in Package Center to see which installed packages depend on it, such as Synology MailPlus Server.\nDo not stop or uninstall it while Synology MailPlus Server is installed.\nTo run a script on a schedule, go to Control Panel > Task Scheduler > Create > Scheduled Task > User-defined script, and call perl with the script's full path.\nKeep scripts in a shared folder that only IT can edit.\",\"Do not uninstall it while Synology MailPlus Server is installed, because MailPlus Server depends on it.\nWrite new scripts in a language SWE maintains, such as Node.js 22, rather than Perl.\",\"Command line, Background service\",\"python2, nodejs-v22, web-station, synology-mailplus-server\",,\"perl, script, scripting, cgi, automation, runtime\",,5.34.1-0301,\nphp-8-2,PHP 8.2,icons/php-8-2.png,Open Source,php.net,Synology Inc.,Development Tools,,IT approval needed,\"phpMyAdmin and Note Station need it, so keep it installed and updated while either of them is installed, until Synology moves those packages to a newer PHP. Security support ends on 31 December 2026, and nothing new should be built on it.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",PHP 8.2 runtime that phpMyAdmin and Note Station need. Keep it updated; build new sites on PHP 8.4.,\"PHP is the open-source scripting language behind many websites. This package comes from php.net and is published by Synology in Package Center; phpMyAdmin and Note Station depend on it, as do the WordPress, Joomla, MediaWiki and vtiger CRM packages. PHP 8.2 gets security fixes only until 31 December 2026.\",\"IT: keep PHP 8.2 installed and updated, because phpMyAdmin and Note Station stop working without it.\nIT: move in-house Web Station sites that use PHP 8.2 to PHP 8.4 before the end of 2026.\nSWE: test internal PHP tools on PHP 8.4 and fix any compatibility problems.\nManagement: Synology decides when phpMyAdmin and Note Station move to a newer PHP. IT tracks this through Package Center updates.\",\"Open Package Center > Installed > PHP 8.2 and install updates when Package Center shows them.\nCheck the package page in Package Center to see which installed packages depend on it, such as phpMyAdmin and Note Station.\nDo not stop or uninstall it while phpMyAdmin, Note Station or another dependent package is installed.\nOpen Main Menu > Web Station > Script Language Settings and note which PHP profiles for in-house sites use PHP 8.2.\nCreate a matching PHP 8.4 profile with the same extensions and settings, then switch each in-house site under Web Service to it and test it.\nKeep phpMyAdmin and Note Station updated. Synology moves them to a newer PHP version through those updates.\",\"Security support ends on 31 December 2026. Use PHP 8.4 (security support until 31 December 2028) for anything built in-house.\nInstall Node.js and PHP updates in a planned maintenance window soon after Package Center shows them.\nPackage Center lists PHP 8.2 as a dependency of phpMyAdmin and Note Station (and of WordPress, Joomla, MediaWiki and vtiger CRM), so installing any of them also installs PHP 8.2. Check which installed packages depend on it before removing it.\",Background service,\"php-8-4, php-8-3, web-station, phpmyadmin, apache-http-server-2-4, note-station, wordpress, joomla, mediawiki, vtigercrm\",,\"php, php 8.2, web scripting, website language, runtime, end of life\",,8.2.30-0170,\nphp-8-3,PHP 8.3,icons/php-8-3.png,Open Source,php.net,Synology Inc.,Development Tools,,IT approval needed,\"Synology publishes it, but it is an open-source runtime for IT and SWE. Use PHP 8.4 where possible, and add 8.3 only for an app that needs it.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",PHP 8.3 for websites on the NAS. Install it only if an app cannot run on PHP 8.4.,PHP is the open-source scripting language behind many websites. This package comes from php.net and is published by Synology in Package Center; it adds PHP 8.3 as a version that Web Station PHP profiles can use. PHP 8.3 gets security fixes until 31 December 2027.,\"SWE: run an internal PHP tool that supports PHP 8.3 but not yet 8.4.\nIT: move a site off PHP 8.2 when the app cannot run on PHP 8.4.\nIT: test an app on PHP 8.3 before a planned move to 8.4.\",\"Confirm the app cannot use PHP 8.4, which is supported for longer.\nInstall PHP 8.3 from Package Center.\nOpen Main Menu > Web Station > Script Language Settings and create a PHP profile that uses PHP 8.3, with the extensions the app needs.\nUnder Web Service, edit the site and select the new profile.\nTest the site, and plan its move to PHP 8.4.\",\"Security support ends on 31 December 2027.\nEvery extra PHP version is one more package to keep updated. Remove it when no site uses it.\",Background service,\"php-8-4, php-8-2, web-station, apache-http-server-2-4\",,\"php, php 8.3, web scripting, website language, runtime\",,8.3.30-0050,\nphp-8-4,PHP 8.4,icons/php-8-4.png,Open Source,php.net,Synology Inc.,Development Tools,,IT approval needed,\"Synology publishes it, but it is an open-source runtime for IT and SWE use only. It is the preferred PHP version for in-house sites.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",\"PHP 8.4 for websites on the NAS. This is the preferred PHP version, with security support to 2028.\",\"PHP is the open-source scripting language behind many websites and web tools. This package comes from php.net and is published by Synology in Package Center; it adds PHP 8.4 as a version that Web Station PHP profiles can use. PHP 8.4 gets security fixes until 31 December 2028, so it is the version to use for in-house PHP sites.\",\"SWE: run internal PHP tools, such as a quotation calculator for Sales, on a supported PHP version.\nIT: move in-house sites off PHP 8.2 before its security support ends on 31 December 2026. Packages such as phpMyAdmin stay on PHP 8.2 until Synology updates them.\nIT: use it as the default PHP version for new Web Station sites.\",\"Open Package Center > Installed > PHP 8.4 and install updates when Package Center shows them. Recent versions also fix loading of the Mailparse and Imagick extensions.\nOpen Main Menu > Web Station > Script Language Settings and create or edit a PHP profile that uses PHP 8.4.\nTurn on only the extensions the site needs, and adjust core settings such as the upload size limit if required.\nUnder Web Service, edit each site and select the PHP 8.4 profile.\nTest each site in a browser and check its error logs.\",\"Security support runs until 31 December 2028.\nInstall Node.js and PHP updates in a planned maintenance window soon after Package Center shows them.\nTurn off display_errors on production sites so error messages do not reveal internal details.\",Background service,\"php-8-3, php-8-2, web-station, mariadb-10, apache-http-server-2-4\",,\"php, php 8.4, web scripting, website language, runtime, latest php\",,8.4.19-0050,\nphpmyadmin,phpMyAdmin,icons/phpmyadmin.png,Open Source,phpMyAdmin devel team,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,IT approval needed,\"Synology publishes it, but it gives full database access, so only IT and SWE use it, and only from the office network.\",IT admin,\"it, swe\",\"Web-based tool for managing MariaDB databases: browse tables, run queries, import and export.\",\"phpMyAdmin is an open-source web tool from the phpMyAdmin team, published by Synology in Package Center, for managing MariaDB and MySQL databases from a browser. IT and developers can browse and edit tables, run SQL queries, manage database users, and export or import data. It needs Web Station and PHP 8.2, and connects to MariaDB 10.\",\"IT: create a separate database user for each internal application, with only the rights it needs.\nSWE: check and fix data in internal tools, such as stock or service-report databases, without command-line tools.\nIT: export a database before an upgrade, so it can be restored if something goes wrong.\",\"Open Main Menu > phpMyAdmin. It opens in a new browser tab.\nSign in with a MariaDB 10 account (not your DSM account).\nSelect a database on the left to browse tables, edit records or run SQL.\nUse the Export tab to save a backup before making changes. Use Import to restore one.\nUnder User accounts, create a separate user for each application and give it access only to its own database.\nLog out when you finish.\",\"Never make phpMyAdmin reachable from the internet. Allow it only from the office network or VPN in Control Panel > Security > Firewall.\nIt needs PHP 8.2. Do not stop or remove PHP 8.2 while phpMyAdmin is installed.\nKnown limitation: after a fresh install or reinstall, the phpMyAdmin icon is visible only to system administrators.\",\"Web portal, DSM web (Main Menu)\",\"mariadb-10, web-station, php-8-2\",\"php-8-2, web-station\",\"phpmyadmin, database admin, mysql, sql, tables, export database, db tool\",,5.2.2-1102,\npython-3-9,Python 3.9,icons/python-3-9.png,Open Source,Python Software Foundation,Synology Inc.,Development Tools,,Not recommended,It reached end-of-life in October 2025. Use a supported Python 3 version in a container instead.,Developer,\"swe, it\",\"Python 3.9 runtime. Support ended in October 2025, so do not install it.\",\"Python is a widely used open-source programming language from the Python Software Foundation, used for scripts, automation and data work. Synology publishes this Python 3.9 package in Package Center. Python 3.9 reached end-of-life in October 2025 and no longer gets security fixes.\",\"SWE: run Python scripts on a supported version (3.12 or later) in Container Manager, not on Python 3.9.\nIT: when moving scripts off Python2, go straight to a supported Python 3 version, not to 3.9.\nEngineering: use data-conversion scripts from SWE, such as test-log converters, that run on a supported Python version.\",\"Do not install Python 3.9 for new work.\nAsk SWE to run scripts on a supported Python 3 version (3.12 or later) in a container through Container Manager, or as a containerized script language website in Web Station.\nKeep each script and its requirements.txt file in a shared folder that is backed up.\nIf an old app really needs 3.9, get IT approval and plan its upgrade at the same time.\",End-of-life since October 2025. There are no more security fixes.,Command line,\"python2, container-manager, web-station, nodejs-v22\",,\"python, python 3.9, python3, script, runtime, end of life\",,3.9.22-0015,\npython2,Python2,icons/python2.png,Open Source,Python Software Foundation,Synology Inc.,Development Tools,,Not recommended,\"It reached end-of-life in January 2020. If it is installed, move scripts to a supported Python 3 version, then remove it once nothing depends on it.\",Developer,\"it, swe\",\"Python 2 runtime. Support ended in January 2020, so move scripts to Python 3 and remove it.\",\"Python is a widely used open-source programming language from the Python Software Foundation; Synology publishes this package in Package Center. It provides Python 2.7.18, the final Python 2 release. Python 2 reached end-of-life in January 2020 and has had no security fixes since then.\",\"IT: find old admin scripts that still run on Python 2 and have them rewritten for Python 3.\nSWE: port Python 2 scripts to a supported Python 3 version (3.12 or later).\nManagement: removing software that has had no support since 2020 lowers the security risk on the NAS.\",\"If Python2 is installed, open Package Center > Installed > Python2 and ask IT to confirm whether another installed package depends on it.\nReview Control Panel > Task Scheduler and the IT and SWE script folders for anything that calls python2.\nPort those scripts to Python 3 and run them on a supported version (3.12 or later), for example in Container Manager.\nRun the new and old versions side by side, compare the results, then switch the scheduled tasks to the new versions.\nOnce nothing uses it, stop and uninstall Python2 from Package Center.\",\"End-of-life since January 2020. Do not use Python 3.9 as the replacement either, because its support also ended, in October 2025.\nDo not uninstall it before checking dependencies. Package Center lists Python2 as a dependency of Download Station, and a scheduled task or script may still need it.\",\"Command line, Background service\",\"python-3-9, container-manager, perl, nodejs-v22, download-station\",,\"python, python 2, python2, script, runtime, end of life, legacy\",,2.7.18-1004,\nvtigercrm,vtigerCRM,icons/vtigercrm.png,Open Source,Vtiger,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Not recommended,\"There is no clear KLAE need for this package, and it depends on PHP 8.2 (security support ends 31 December 2026). Management should choose any company CRM with vendor support.\",IT admin,\"sales, it\",\"Open-source CRM for leads, contacts and deals. It is not approved as KLAE's customer system.\",\"vtiger CRM is an open-source customer relationship management (CRM) system from Vtiger for tracking leads, contacts, deals, quotes and support tickets, published by Synology in Package Center. Staff use it in a web browser. It needs Web Station, Apache HTTP Server 2.4, PHP 8.2 and MariaDB 10.\",\"Sales: do not keep customer records here. Ask Management which CRM or customer list is approved.\nSales: until then, keep customer contacts in Synology Contacts and quotations in Synology Drive.\nIT: avoid holding commercially sensitive customer and pricing data in an unsupported web application.\",\"Do not install it without written approval from Management and IT.\nIf Sales needs a CRM, raise a request so IT and Management can compare supported options (cost, support and where the data is stored).\nIf it is approved, install vtiger CRM from Package Center (it also installs Web Station, Apache HTTP Server 2.4, PHP 8.2 and MariaDB 10) and follow the wizard.\nSign in as the administrator, create user accounts and roles for Sales, and allow access only from the office network or VPN.\nBack up its database regularly and keep the package updated.\",\"Customer lists, prices and quotations are commercially sensitive. They need a supported system with proper access control and backups.\nIt needs PHP 8.2, whose security support ends on 31 December 2026.\",Web portal,\"synology-contacts, synology-drive-server, web-station, mariadb-10, php-8-2, apache-http-server-2-4\",\"apache-http-server-2-4, mariadb-10, php-8-2, web-station\",\"crm, vtiger, customer database, leads, sales pipeline, contacts, deals\",,8.0.0-1203,\nwordpress,WordPress,icons/wordpress.png,Open Source,WordPress,Synology Inc.,Utilities,,Not recommended,Keep the company website with a managed web host. Running WordPress on the NAS that holds company files adds security risk.,IT admin,\"marketing, it\",Open-source website and blog builder. KLAE's website should not run on the NAS.,\"WordPress is the most widely used open-source content management system for websites and blogs; Synology publishes the package in Package Center. Editors manage pages, posts and plugins from a browser dashboard. It needs Web Station, Apache HTTP Server 2.4, PHP 8.2 and MariaDB 10.\",\"Marketing: keep the public KLAE website and product pages with an external managed web host, not on the office NAS.\nMarketing: if you need to preview a website redesign, ask IT about a temporary test copy that only the office network can reach.\nIT: avoid exposing the NAS to the internet through a public website and its plugins.\",\"Do not install it for the public website. Talk to IT about the external host instead.\nIf IT approves an internal test copy, note that Package Center also installs what it needs: Web Station, Apache HTTP Server 2.4, PHP 8.2 and MariaDB 10.\nInstall WordPress from Package Center and follow the wizard, which asks for MariaDB 10 details to create its database.\nOpen the site in a browser, finish the WordPress setup and create a separate editor account for each user.\nAllow access only from the office network, and delete the test copy when the project ends.\",\"Plugins and themes are the most common way WordPress sites get hacked. Install only well-known ones and keep them updated.\nNever forward web ports from the office router to the NAS for a WordPress site.\nIt needs PHP 8.2, whose security support ends on 31 December 2026.\",Web portal,\"joomla, mediawiki, web-station, mariadb-10, php-8-2, apache-http-server-2-4\",\"apache-http-server-2-4, mariadb-10, php-8-2, web-station\",\"wordpress, website, blog, cms, web pages, company website, site builder\",,6.8.6-1506,\n",
  "departments": "id,name,description\nmanagement,Management,\"Directors and managers. Oversight of company data, access, reporting and business continuity.\"\nsales,Sales & Business Development,\"Quotations, tenders, customer files and principals' price lists, at HQ and the regional offices.\"\nmarketing,Marketing,\"Brochures, catalogues, product photos and videos, website and exhibition material.\"\nengineering,Engineering & Technical,\"Product specialists, application and field service engineers, projects, commissioning and the training centre.\"\nprocurement,\"Procurement, Logistics & Warehouse\",\"Purchase orders, supplier documents, stock records, shipping and delivery paperwork.\"\nfinance,Finance & Accounts,\"Invoices, payments, statements, audit files and financial reports.\"\nhr,HR & Admin,\"Staff records, policies, forms, leave, office administration and facilities.\"\nswe,Software Engineering,Developers who build and run internal software and tools.\nit,IT / System Administration,\"Runs the NAS, user accounts, backups, security and network services.\"\n",
  "tasks": "group,task,description,apps\nEveryday work,Save and share files with my team,Team folders you can open from HQ and every regional office.,\"synology-drive-server, file-station\"\nEveryday work,Open office files from home or a regional office,Work away from your desk without emailing files to yourself.,\"synology-drive-server, quickconnect, vpn-server\"\nEveryday work,Send a large file to a customer or supplier,Share a download link instead of a big email attachment.,\"synology-drive-server, file-station\"\nEveryday work,Edit a document or spreadsheet together,Several people work on the same file at the same time.,\"synology-office, synology-drive-server\"\nEveryday work,Find a file I saved somewhere,Search file names and contents across the NAS.,universal-search\nEveryday work,Keep site and product photos organised,Upload from your phone and sort into shared albums.,synology-photos\nEveryday work,\"Company email, calendar and chat\",\"Mail, meetings and messages hosted on our own NAS.\",\"synology-mailplus-server, synology-mailplus, synology-calendar, synology-chat-server\"\nBackup & recovery,Back up my PC or laptop,Especially laptops that travel to customer sites.,active-backup-for-business\nBackup & recovery,Get back a file I deleted or overwrote,Restore an earlier version or recover from the recycle bin.,\"synology-drive-server, snapshot-replication\"\nBackup & recovery,Keep an offsite copy of company data,\"Protection against disk failure, fire, theft and ransomware.\",\"hyper-backup, hyper-backup-vault, snapshot-replication\"\nBackup & recovery,Back up Microsoft 365 or Google Workspace,\"Mailboxes, OneDrive or Google Drive, calendars and contacts.\",\"active-backup-for-microsoft-365, active-backup-for-google-workspace\"\nBackup & recovery,Copy files to or from a USB drive,Plug in a drive and copy automatically.,usb-copy\nIT & development,Sign in more securely,Two-step sign-in with phone approval or a security key.,secure-signin-service\nIT & development,Watch office or warehouse cameras,Record and review CCTV footage.,surveillance-station\nIT & development,Host an internal website or web app,Run intranet pages and internal tools on the NAS.,\"web-station, container-manager\"\nIT & development,Keep source code in a private Git server,Company code stays on company hardware.,git-server\nIT & development,Use AI features in Office and MailPlus,\"Connect an approved AI provider, controlled by IT.\",synology-ai-console\nIT & development,Check NAS health and disk space,\"Disk status, free space and alerts.\",\"storage-manager, storage-analyzer, active-insight\"\n",
  "glossary": "term,meaning\nNAS,Network Attached Storage. Our Synology NAS is a file server on the office network. It stores shared files and runs the packages in this guide.\nDSM,\"DiskStation Manager, the operating system of the NAS. You sign in to DSM in a web browser to open apps such as File Station.\"\nPackage Center,\"The app store inside DSM. IT installs, updates and removes packages from here.\"\nPackage,An app or service installed on the NAS from Package Center.\nShared folder,\"A top-level folder on the NAS, for example \"\"Sales\"\" or \"\"Finance\"\". IT decides who can read or change each one.\"\nDSM account,Your username and password for the NAS. It may be the same as your Windows or domain sign-in.\nQuickConnect,Synology's relay service. It lets Synology apps reach our NAS from outside the office without opening ports on the router.\nVPN,\"An encrypted tunnel from your laptop to the office network, so you can use internal services from home or a regional office.\"\nSMB,\"The Windows file-sharing protocol. It lets you open a NAS shared folder as a network drive in Windows, for example drive Z.\"\nWebDAV,A way to open NAS files over the web (HTTP/HTTPS). Some apps and mobile file managers use it.\nSnapshot,\"A read-only, point-in-time copy of a shared folder. Used to restore files quickly after a mistake or a ransomware attack.\"\nBackup task,\"A scheduled job that copies data somewhere else: another NAS, a USB drive or a cloud service.\"\n3-2-1 rule,\"Keep 3 copies of important data, on 2 different types of storage, with 1 copy offsite.\"\nRAID / SHR,Ways of combining disks so the NAS keeps working when one disk fails. RAID is not a backup: deleted or encrypted files are lost on every disk at once.\nVolume,A storage area built from the NAS disks. Shared folders live on volumes.\n2-step sign-in (2FA),\"Signing in with your password plus a second check, such as an approval on your phone or a security key.\"\nLDAP / Active Directory,Central user directories. They let one username and password work across many systems.\nContainer,A packaged app that runs isolated on the NAS through Container Manager (Docker).\nLicence,\"Some packages need paid licences for extra users, mailboxes, cameras or features.\"\nEnd of life (EOL),Software that no longer gets security fixes. It should be upgraded or removed.\n",
  "faq": "question,answer\nCan I install a package myself?,\"No. IT installs and configures packages so that security, licences and storage stay under control. If your team needs a package, send a request to IT with the business reason.\"\nWhy do we avoid third-party (community) packages?,\"Packages from third-party publishers can stop being updated without warning, may not get security fixes, and are not supported by Synology. Management has decided to use packages published by Synology Inc. wherever possible. Every package in this guide is published by Synology Inc. through the official Package Center.\"\nAre the Open Source packages third-party apps?,\"Not in the sense the policy means. They are built by open-source projects (for example php.net, nodejs.org or Docker Inc.), but Synology Inc. packages, signs and publishes them in the official Package Center and ships their updates. They are developer tools, so only IT and Software Engineering use them, with IT approval.\"\nWhat is the difference between Synology Drive and File Station?,\"Synology Drive is for everyday work: it syncs folders to your PC, shares links, keeps version history and has a mobile app. File Station is the file manager inside DSM, mostly used in the browser. If you are not sure, use Synology Drive.\"\nI deleted or overwrote a file by mistake. What do I do?,\"In Synology Drive, check the file's version history or the Recycle Bin first. If it is not there, contact IT as soon as possible. IT may be able to restore it from a snapshot or a backup.\"\nHow do I work from home or from a regional office?,\"Use the Synology Drive desktop or mobile app with the address IT gives you. For other internal systems, IT can set you up with VPN.\"\nMy account is locked or I forgot my password.,\"Contact IT. For your security, IT will never ask for your password by chat or email.\"\nHow do I share a file with a customer safely?,\"Create a sharing link in Synology Drive, set an expiry date and, for sensitive files, a password. Do not share whole folders outside the company unless IT agrees.\"\nWho keeps this guide up to date?,\"IT. If something is wrong or missing, use the details under Contact IT.\"\n"
};
